      "name": "BinkFileBufferedRead",
      "signature": "DWORD BinkFileBufferedRead(BinkFileHandle * pBinkFile, DWORD dwSeekPosition, DWORD dwRequestedPosition, BYTE * pBuffer, DWORD nBytesToRead)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "DWORD",
      "comment": "Performs buffered file reading for Bink video streams with automatic seeking and rate limiting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize seek state and start timing with timeGetTime()\n2. If requested position differs from current position, set seek required flag\n3. Increment reference counter and wait for any pending BinkService operations\n4. If seek within buffer range, adjust buffer pointers and update statistics\n5. If seek outside buffer range, use SetFilePointer and reset buffer state\n6. Copy available data from internal buffer to output buffer using optimized DWORD+byte copy loops\n7. If more data needed, perform direct file read with ReadFile and apply rate limiting\n8. Update file statistics and calculate next buffer prefetch parameters\n9. Return total elapsed time for performance monitoring\n\nParameters:\npBinkFile - Pointer to BinkFileHandle structure containing file state and buffers\ndwSeekPosition - Unused parameter (reserved for future seeking functionality)  \ndwRequestedPosition - File position to seek to, or 0xFFFFFFFF to continue from current position\npBuffer - Output buffer to receive read data\nnBytesToRead - Number of bytes to read into output buffer\n\nReturns:\nElapsed time in milliseconds since function start (for performance profiling)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf dwRequestedPosition is 0xFFFFFFFF, no seeking is performed\nIf rate limiter is configured (offset +0x7C), enforces maximum bytes/second throughput\nZero-length reads immediately return with timing information\nBuffer wraparound is handled by resetting to base pointer at offset +0x64\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1000 - Minimum buffer prefetch size (4096 bytes)\n0xFFFFFFFF - Special value indicating no seek operation required\n100 (0x64) - Offset to buffer base pointer in BinkFileHandle structure\n\nBinkFileHandle Structure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type        Description\n+0x18   4     pBinkService        void*       Pointer to Bink service object\n+0x20   4     dwTotalBytesRead    DWORD       Total bytes read from file\n+0x28   4     dwReadTime          DWORD       Cumulative file read time\n+0x2C   4     dwElapsedTime       DWORD       Total function elapsed time\n+0x38   4     dwBufferSize        DWORD       Internal buffer size limit\n+0x40   4     dwPrefetchSize      DWORD       Next buffer prefetch amount\n+0x44   4     dwAvailableBytes    DWORD       Bytes available in buffer\n+0x48   4     hFile               HANDLE      Win32 file handle\n+0x4C   4     dwFileHighPosition  DWORD       High water mark file position\n+0x50   4     dwCurrentPosition   DWORD       Current file position\n+0x54   4     pBufferPointer      void*       Current buffer read pointer\n+0x58   4     dwBytesProcessed    DWORD       Total bytes processed\n+0x5C   1     byReferenceCounter  byte        Thread reference counter\n+0x60   4     dwServiceFlag       DWORD       BinkService operation flag\n+0x64   4     pBufferBase         void*       Base of circular buffer\n+0x68   4     pBufferEnd          void*       End of circular buffer\n+0x6C   4     dwBufferManagement  DWORD       Buffer management state\n+0x74   4     dwFileBaseOffset    DWORD       File offset adjustment\n+0x78   4     dwFileEndPosition   DWORD       End of file position\n+0x7C   4     dwRateLimit         DWORD       Rate limiting (bytes/second, 0=disabled)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
