      "name": "BinkBufferLock",
      "signature": "int BinkBufferLock(BinkBuffer * pBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Locks a Bink video buffer for direct pixel access via DirectDraw surface locking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pBuffer parameter (null check returns 0)\n2. Retrieve DirectDraw surface pointer from pBuffer->field_0x14[0x12]\n3. If no surface, check fallback mode and copy buffer pointers from fallback location\n4. Initialize 108-byte lock parameters structure with size 0x6c\n5. If cursor checking enabled, save cursor state with BinkCheckCursor\n6. Attempt DirectDraw surface lock via IDirectDraw->Lock(surface, 0, lockParams)\n7. On lock failure, set error flag 0x80000000 and call IDirectDraw->Restore()\n8. Retry lock operation with additional parameters until success\n9. Store locked surface pointer in pBuffer[1].dwFlags from lockParams[16]\n10. Calculate memory pointer based on windowed vs fullscreen mode\n11. For fullscreen: pointer = screenY * stride + basePtr + screenX * videoMemory\n12. For windowed: pointer = surfacePtr directly\n13. Store final pointer and stride in pBuffer->field_0x14[0] and [1]\n\nParameters:\npBuffer: Pointer to BinkBuffer structure containing video buffer configuration\n         - field_0x14: Surface and pointer storage area\n         - dwScreenX/dwScreenY: Screen coordinates for buffer positioning  \n         - dwFlags: Status flags including error bit 0x80000000\n         - hWnd: Window handle (0 for fullscreen mode)\n\nReturns:\n1: Success - buffer locked and pointers configured\n0: Failure - null buffer, lock failed, or DirectDraw error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null pBuffer parameter: immediate return 0\n- No DirectDraw surface: fallback to buffer copy mode\n- Lock failure with cursor check: restores cursor before exit\n- Windowed mode: direct surface pointer without coordinate calculation\n- Fullscreen mode: calculated pointer with stride and video memory offset\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6c: Size of DirectDraw lock parameters structure (108 bytes)\n0x80000000: Error flag bit set in pBuffer->dwFlags on lock failure  \n0x12: Offset in pBuffer->field_0x14 where DirectDraw surface pointer stored\n0x23: Offset for fallback mode check flag\n0x24/0x25: Offsets for fallback buffer source pointers\n0x1c: Offset for cursor check enable flag\n100: Offset in IDirectDraw vtable for Lock() method  \n0x6c: Offset in IDirectDraw vtable for Restore() method\n\nError Handling:\n- Lock failure triggers Restore() call and retry loop\n- Error flag 0x80000000 set in dwFlags on persistent failure\n- Cursor state restored if lock fails and cursor checking was enabled\n- Returns 0 on any critical failure (null buffer, persistent lock error)\n\nStructure Layout:\nBinkBuffer fields accessed:\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type              Description\n0x00    4     field_0x0     void*            Base buffer pointer\n0x04    4     field_0x4     void*            Secondary buffer info  \n0x14    4     field_0x14    void*            Surface pointer storage\n0x10    4     dwFlags       int              Status and error flags\n0x?     4     dwScreenX     int              X coordinate on screen\n0x?     4     dwScreenY     int              Y coordinate on screen  \n0x?     4     hWnd          int              Window handle (0=fullscreen)",
