      "name": "BinkFileGetSize",
      "signature": "void BinkFileGetSize(int nBinkFile)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Synchronizes access to Bink file handle and performs cleanup operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment reference counter at offset 0x5c (thread-safe with LOCK/UNLOCK)\n2. Read status flag from offset 0x60 and enter wait loop if non-zero\n3. While status is active: yield thread with Sleep(0) and call BinkService for processing\n4. Exit wait loop when status becomes zero (operation completed)\n5. Check cleanup flag at offset 0x70, if zero then close file handle at offset 0x48\n6. Decrement reference counter at offset 0x5c (thread-safe with LOCK/UNLOCK)\n\nParameters:\n  pBinkFile (int): Pointer to BinkFileHandle structure containing file state and handles\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Reference counter prevents concurrent access during critical operations\n  - Status polling with Sleep(0) yields CPU to allow other threads to complete work\n  - Conditional handle cleanup based on internal flag state\n  - LOCK/UNLOCK primitives ensure atomic reference counter operations\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type      | Description\n-------|------|---------------|-----------|------------------------------------------\n0x18   | 4    | pServiceData  | void*     | Pointer to data passed to BinkService\n0x48   | 4    | hFile         | HANDLE    | File handle for Bink resource\n0x5c   | 1    | bRefCounter   | byte      | Thread-safe reference counter\n0x60   | 4    | dwStatus      | uint      | Status/completion flag (0=done)\n0x70   | 4    | dwCleanupFlag | uint      | Cleanup control flag (0=close handle)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
