      "name": "BinkPause",
      "signature": "int BinkPause(BinkDecoder * pBinkDecoder, int nPauseState)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Controls Bink video playback pause state and synchronizes timing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pBinkDecoder is not NULL, return 0 if invalid\n2. Get current system time using timeGetTime() API\n3. Adjust playback timing for the decoder with current timestamp\n4. Execute decoder-specific timing function FUN_10009b70\n5. If transitioning from paused to playing (nPauseState=0 and was paused), clear frame buffer flag at offset 0x20C\n6. Store new pause state in decoder at offset 0xFC\n7. If audio processor is active (offset 0x1E8 != -1), invoke audio callback function with pause state\n8. Clear frame processing flag at offset 0x360\n9. If audio processor still active, process current Bink frame for display\n10. Return the current pause state from decoder\n\nParameters:\npBinkDecoder - Pointer to BinkDecoder structure containing video state and buffers\nnPauseState - Pause control flag (0=resume playback, non-zero=pause playback)\n\nReturns:\nCurrent pause state from decoder (matches nPauseState parameter when successful)\nReturns 0 if pBinkDecoder is NULL (error condition)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nTransition from paused to playing state clears frame buffer synchronization flag\nAudio processor callbacks are conditionally executed based on availability\nFrame processing occurs only when audio system is active\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xFC (252) - Pause state flag storage offset in decoder structure\n0x3F (63) - Pause state flag storage offset (alternate location)  \n0x83 (131) - Frame buffer synchronization flag offset\n0x7A (122) - Audio processor availability flag offset (-1 = disabled)\n0xAE (174) - Audio callback function pointer offset\n0xA9 (169) - Audio callback parameter base offset\n0xD8 (216) - Frame processing flag offset\n0x20C (524) - Frame buffer flag storage offset",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
