      "name": "InitializeBinkAudioContext",
      "signature": "uint * InitializeBinkAudioContext(uint dwVideoWidth, uint dwVideoHeight, uint dwConfigFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint *",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a Bink audio context for video decoding with FFT processing capabilities.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate total sample pairs needed (dwVideoWidth * dwVideoHeight + 1) >> 1\n2. Determine memory size based on config flags: base 0x2688 + ((~dwConfigFlags & 1) << 1 | 1) * 0x2000\n3. Allocate context buffer using RadMalloc, return NULL on failure\n4. Zero-initialize first 0x9a2 uint entries (9,890 bytes) in the context buffer\n5. Set up buffer pointers: offset 0x10 points to buffer+0x9a2, offset 0xc points to buffer+0x11a2\n6. Set magic constant 0x3000 at offset 0x2684 (context[0x9a1])\n7. Calculate base sample count based on video width: if width < 44100 then use conditional value else 0x800\n8. Apply conditional scaling: if width < 22050 use (base & 0xfffffe00) + 0x400 else base + 0x400\n9. Calculate total samples = base * height, store divided by 16 at offset 8, store full value at offset 0\n10. Calculate FFT normalization factor using g_flFftConstant / sqrt(total samples), store at offset 4\n11. Process frequency table g_adFrequencyTable[25] to initialize band coefficients\n12. For each frequency entry, if sample pairs <= frequency: store (frequency * samples/2) / sample pairs\n13. Store number of processed frequency bands at offset 0x18, store samples/2 at final band offset\n14. Initialize flags: set offset 0x84 = 0, offset 0x14 = 1\n15. Return pointer to initialized context buffer\n\nParameters:\ndwVideoWidth (uint): Video frame width in pixels, affects sample rate calculation (0x5622/0xac44 thresholds)\ndwVideoHeight (uint): Video frame height in pixels, multiplied with width for total sample calculation  \ndwConfigFlags (uint): Configuration flags, bit 0 inverted affects memory allocation size\n\nReturns:\nuint *: Pointer to allocated and initialized Bink audio context (9,890+ uint entries)\nNULL: Memory allocation failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\nWidth < 22050 (0x5622): Uses reduced sample rate with 0x400 base addition\nWidth >= 44100 (0xac44): Uses maximum sample rate 0x800\nSample pairs > frequency table entry: Skip coefficient calculation for that band\nMemory allocation failure: Returns NULL immediately without cleanup\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x2688 (9864): Base context structure size in bytes\n0x2000 (8192): Additional buffer size unit based on config flags\n0x9a2 (2466): Number of uint entries to zero-initialize (9864 bytes)\n0x11a2 (4514): Secondary buffer offset from base\n0x3000 (12288): Magic constant stored at context[0x9a1]\n0x5622 (22050): Low sample rate threshold for conditional processing\n0xac44 (44100): High sample rate threshold for maximum rate\n0x400 (1024): Base sample count addition for conditional rates\n0x800 (2048): Maximum sample count for high width values\n0x84 (132): Byte offset for flags initialization (context[0x21] * 4)\n0x14 (20): Byte offset for enable flag (context[0x5] * 4)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type    Description\n0x00    4     dwBaseSampleCount    uint    Base sample count (width-dependent)\n0x04    4     dwFftNormalization   uint    FFT normalization factor from sqrt calculation\n0x08    4     dwSamplesDiv16       uint    Total samples divided by 16\n0x0c    4     pSecondaryBuffer     uint    Pointer to buffer + 0x11a2 offset\n0x10    4     pPrimaryBuffer       uint    Pointer to buffer + 0x9a2 offset  \n0x14    4     dwEnableFlag         uint    Enable flag (set to 1)\n0x18    4     dwFrequencyBands     uint    Number of processed frequency bands\n0x1c    60    adBandCoefficients   uint[15] Frequency band coefficient array\n0x84    4     dwProcessingFlags    uint    Processing flags (initialized to 0)\n...     ...   ...                  ...     Additional context data continues\n0x2684  4     dwMagicConstant      uint    Magic constant 0x3000",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
