      "name": "ConvertExtendedFloatWithConfig",
      "signature": "void ConvertExtendedFloatWithConfig(ExtendedFloat * pExtendedFloat, uint * pOutputData)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts extended precision floating point data to standard format with predefined configuration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push predefined conversion configuration (DAT_1002e920) onto stack\n2. Push output data pointer onto stack  \n3. Push extended float input pointer onto stack\n4. Call ConvertExtendedFloat with the three parameters\n5. Clean up stack (12 bytes total for 3 parameters)\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pExtendedFloat - Pointer to ExtendedFloat structure containing source data\n  pOutputData    - Pointer to uint buffer for converted output data\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, output written directly to pOutputData buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Uses hardcoded configuration at 0x1002e920 for all conversions\n  Acts as wrapper to simplify calls to ConvertExtendedFloat with standard config\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1002e920 - Address of predefined ConversionConfig structure\n  0xc        - Stack cleanup size (12 bytes for 3 parameters)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
