      "name": "BinkFileSeek",
      "signature": "uint BinkFileSeek(BinkFileHandle * pFileHandle, uint dwPosition)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Performs page-aligned seeking in a Bink video file with thread synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment lock counter at file handle offset 0x5c using atomic operation\n2. Wait for any pending I/O operations by polling busy flag at offset 0x60\n3. While busy flag is non-zero, yield thread with Sleep(0) and service Bink queue\n4. Decrement lock counter using atomic operation when I/O completes\n5. Return page-aligned position by masking to 4KB boundaries\n\nParameters:\npFileHandle (BinkFileHandle *): Pointer to Bink file handle structure containing synchronization state\nnPosition (uint): Target file position in bytes to seek to\n\nReturns:\nuint: Page-aligned position (4KB boundary) calculated as (nPosition + 0xFFF) & 0xFFFFF000\n\nSpecial Cases:\nUses atomic increment/decrement operations (LOCK prefix) for thread safety\nSleep(0) yields CPU time slice while waiting for I/O completion\nBinkService call processes queued operations during wait\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x5c (92): Offset to lock counter byte in BinkFileHandle structure\n0x60 (96): Offset to busy flag dword in BinkFileHandle structure  \n0x18 (24): Offset to service queue pointer in BinkFileHandle structure\n0xFFF (4095): Page size mask for rounding up to next 4KB boundary\n0xFFFFF000: Page alignment mask for 4KB boundaries",
