      "name": "BinkSetIOSize",
      "signature": "void BinkSetIOSize(uint dwIOSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets the I/O buffer size for Bink video codec operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store the specified buffer size in the global Bink I/O size variable\n\nParameters:\n  dwIOSize (uint): Buffer size in bytes to use for Bink I/O operations\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Buffer size is stored globally and affects all subsequent Bink operations\n  - Default buffer size (0xFFFFFFFF) indicates no specific size limit\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  None",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
