      "name": "SetFpuControlWordConditional",
      "signature": "void SetFpuControlWordConditional(ushort wControlWord)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Conditionally sets FPU control word if it differs from default precision control\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare parameter control word with 0x27f (default 64-bit precision control)\n2. If values match, skip FPU control word update and return immediately\n3. If values differ, load new control word into FPU control register using FLDCW\n4. Clean up stack parameter and return\n\nParameters:\nwControlWord (ushort) - 16-bit FPU control word value to conditionally set\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- 0x27f (639 decimal): Default FPU control word for 64-bit precision, round to nearest\n- Control word format: bits 8-9 precision control (00=24-bit, 10=53-bit, 11=64-bit)\n- Control word format: bits 10-11 rounding control (00=nearest, 01=down, 10=up, 11=truncate)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x27f (639) - Default FPU control word: 64-bit precision + round to nearest\n\nNote: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary variable optimized away by decompiler",
