      "name": "CreateDirectDrawSurface",
      "signature": "int CreateDirectDrawSurface(dword dwFormat, dword dwWidthCopy, dword dwHeightCopy)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Creates DirectDraw surface with specified format and dimensions\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize surface descriptor structure (DDSURFACEDESC) with zeros\n2. Set surface flags based on format: 0x840 for standard format, 0x3C40 for high color\n3. Set surface type (0x6c = DDSD_CAPS | DDSD_HEIGHT | DDSD_WIDTH | DDSD_PIXELFORMAT)\n4. Set pixel format (0x7 for standard, 0x1007 for high color formats)\n5. Copy width and height parameters to surface descriptor\n6. If format > 16, configure high color mode (32 bits per pixel, depth of 4)\n7. Call DirectDraw CreateSurface method via vtable offset 0x18\n8. Create surface using parameters via vtable offset 0x64 (100 decimal)\n9. Clear surface buffer with specified format using ClearVideoBufferByFormat\n10. Lock surface for rendering via vtable offset 0x80 (128 decimal)\n\nParameters:\ndwFormat - Surface format identifier (1 = standard, >16 = high color formats)\ndwWidth - Surface width in pixels\ndwHeight - Surface height in pixels\n\nReturns:\n0 - Error occurred during DirectDraw operations\ndwReturnValue - Success handle/identifier for created surface\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFormat 1 uses standard color mode with flags 0x840\nFormats > 16 use high color mode with flags 0x3C40 and 32 bits per pixel\nDirectDraw interface failures return 0 immediately\nSurface creation failures clean up and return 0\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6c (108) - Surface descriptor size/type flags\n0x7 - Standard pixel format identifier  \n0x1007 (4103) - High color pixel format identifier\n0x840 (2112) - Standard surface flags (0x800 | 0x40)\n0x3C40 (15424) - High color surface flags (0x3800 | 0x800 | 0x40)\n0x20 (32) - Bits per pixel for high color mode\n0x4 - Bytes per pixel for high color mode\n0x18 (24) - DirectDraw CreateSurface vtable offset\n0x64 (100) - Surface creation method vtable offset\n0x80 (128) - Surface lock method vtable offset\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field           Type     Description\n0x00    4     dwSize          dword    Structure size (0x6c)\n0x04    4     dwFlags         dword    Surface capability flags\n0x08    4     dwHeight        dword    Surface height in pixels\n0x0C    4     dwWidth         dword    Surface width in pixels  \n0x10    4     dwLinearSize    dword    Surface pitch/linear size\n0x14    4     dwBackBuffer    dword    Back buffer count\n0x18    4     dwMipMapCount   dword    Mipmap levels\n0x1C    4     dwAlphaBitDepth dword    Alpha bit depth\n0x20    4     dwReserved      dword    Reserved field\n0x24    4     lpSurface       ptr      Surface memory pointer\n0x28    8     ddckColorKey    struct   Color key structure\n0x30    32    ddpfPixelFormat struct   Pixel format structure\n0x50    16    ddsCaps         struct   Surface capabilities\n0x60    12    reserved        bytes    Reserved space",
