      "name": "ClassifyFloatingPointIntegerType",
      "signature": "undefined4 ClassifyFloatingPointIntegerType(double dValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Classifies floating-point number as integer or fractional with divisibility check.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_1002136b to classify the floating-point value's special cases (NaN, infinity, denormal)\n2. Check classification result flags: if (dwClassification & 0x90) == 0, proceed to integer test\n3. Round input value using __frnd and compare with original to test if already integer\n4. If value is integer, perform divisibility test by dividing by global constant _DAT_10027f70\n5. Round quotient and compare with unrounded quotient to determine exact divisibility\n6. Return 2 if exactly divisible, 1 if integer but not divisible, 0 if not integer or special case\n\nParameters:\n- param_1 (double): Input floating-point value to classify\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Value is not an integer, or is NaN/infinity/denormal (special case)\n- 1: Value is an integer but not exactly divisible by constant _DAT_10027f70  \n- 2: Value is an integer and exactly divisible by constant _DAT_10027f70\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NaN, infinity, denormal numbers return 0 (detected by FUN_1002136b)\n- Floating-point precision limits may affect very large integer values\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x90: Bit mask for floating-point classification flags (special number indicators)\n- _DAT_10027f70: Global divisibility constant (0x4000000000000000 = 2.0 in IEEE 754)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
