      "name": "ValidateLogarithmDomain",
      "signature": "int ValidateLogarithmDomain(int nMantissaLow, int nMantissaHigh, double dInput, double * pdResult)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Validates logarithm domain and handles special floating-point cases.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Combine 32-bit mantissa parts (nMantissaLow, nMantissaHigh) into 64-bit value\n2. Apply absolute value if combined mantissa is negative\n3. Check for infinity in input parameter (0x7FF00000 in upper bits)\n4. Handle NaN case: if lower bits non-zero, proceed to special value logic\n5. Validate mantissa against pi constant boundary for domain checking  \n6. Handle negative infinity input: validate against pi boundary\n7. Process special mantissa values: +infinity (0x7FF00000) and -infinity (0xFFF00000)\n8. For -infinity mantissa, call sign check function and apply conditional negation\n9. Compare input against zero constant for branch logic\n10. Set result to appropriate mathematical constant or computed value\n11. Store final result through pointer and return status code\n\nParameters:\nnMantissaLow (int): Lower 32 bits of 64-bit mantissa value\nnMantissaHigh (int): Upper 32 bits of 64-bit mantissa value  \ndInput (double): Input value for logarithm domain validation\npdResult (double *): Pointer to store computed result value\n\nReturns:\n0: Standard computation path, result stored in *pdResult\n1: Special case handled, NaN constant stored in *pdResult\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Input infinity with non-zero mantissa: branches to special value handler\n- Mantissa positive infinity with zero lower bits: domain boundary check\n- Mantissa negative infinity with zero lower bits: calls sign validation\n- Input negative infinity: validates against pi boundary\n- Domain validation uses pi constant (3.14159...) as boundary threshold\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x7FF00000: IEEE 754 positive infinity bit pattern (upper 32 bits)\n0xFFF00000: IEEE 754 negative infinity bit pattern (upper 32 bits) \n0x100000: Bit pattern for mantissa boundary checking\n\nError Handling:\nReturns 0 for invalid combinations (non-zero lower bits with infinity mantissa)\nReturns 0 for out-of-domain inputs after setting appropriate result\nReturns 1 only for specific NaN result case\n\nMathematical Constants:\ng_dZeroConstant: Double precision zero (0.0) for comparisons\ng_dPositiveInfinity: IEEE 754 positive infinity constant  \ng_dNegativeZero: IEEE 754 negative zero (-0.0)\ng_dNaNConstant: IEEE 754 Not-a-Number constant\ng_dPiConstant: Mathematical pi constant for domain validation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
