      "name": "ProcessAudioSampleInterpolation",
      "signature": "void ProcessAudioSampleInterpolation(BinkAudioProcessor * pProcessor, uint * pOutputBuffer, uint * pOutputSize, uint dwParam4, uint * pResultValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Performs audio sample interpolation and data buffer copying for Bink video/audio processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get timestamp value from auxiliary function call\n2. Check processing flag at offset 0x14 - if set, clear it and skip interpolation\n3. If processing flag is clear, perform sample interpolation:\n   a. Load sample count from offset 0x8\n   b. Get source sample data pointer from offset 0x10\n   c. Get destination buffer pointer at offset 0x2484 (base + 0x921*4)\n   d. For each sample index 0 to sampleCount-1:\n      - Calculate weighted interpolation: new = ((count-index)*newSample + index*oldSample) / count\n      - Store interpolated result back to sample buffer\n      - Advance to next sample (increment by 2 bytes)\n4. Calculate buffer copy size: sampleCount * 2 bytes\n5. Calculate source address: basePointer + (baseValue - sampleCount) * 2\n6. Copy data from calculated source to internal buffer at offset 0x2484 using optimized DWORD copy\n7. Set output parameters if non-NULL:\n   - pOutputSize: (sampleCount * 0x7fffffff + baseValue) * 2\n   - pOutputBuffer: sample data pointer from offset 0x10\n   - pResultValue: timestamp + dwParam4\n\nParameters:\npProcessor (BinkAudioProcessor *): Main audio processing structure containing sample data and control fields\npOutputBuffer (uint *): Optional output pointer to receive sample buffer address (can be NULL)\npOutputSize (uint *): Optional output pointer to receive calculated buffer size (can be NULL)\ndwParam4 (uint): Parameter value added to timestamp for result calculation\npResultValue (uint *): Optional output pointer to receive timestamp + dwParam4 (can be NULL)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name        | Type      | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwBaseValue      | uint      | Base value used in size calculation\n0x04   | 4    | dwBytePointer    | uint      | Byte-level pointer base\n0x08   | 4    | dwSampleCount    | uint      | Number of audio samples to process\n0x0C   | 4    | dwUnused1        | uint      | Unused field\n0x10   | 4    | pSampleData      | short *   | Pointer to audio sample buffer\n0x14   | 4    | dwProcessingFlag | uint      | Processing control flag (0=interpolate, 1=skip)\n0x18   | 9220 | abDataBuffer     | byte[]    | Internal processing buffer at offset 0x2484\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If dwProcessingFlag is non-zero, interpolation is skipped and flag is cleared\n- Output parameters are only set if pointer is non-NULL\n- Buffer copy uses optimized DWORD transfer followed by byte-level remainder\n- Sample interpolation uses weighted average: ((n-i)*new + i*old) / n\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x921 (2337): DWORD offset to internal buffer (0x921 * 4 = 0x2484 bytes)\n0x2484 (9252): Byte offset to internal data buffer\n0x7fffffff: Large multiplier used in output size calculation (2147483647)\n2: Bytes per audio sample (16-bit samples)",
