      "name": "FormatFloatingPointWithState",
      "signature": "void FormatFloatingPointWithState(uint dwFormatFlags, char * lpszOutputBuffer, size_t dwBufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Formats floating point values with global state tracking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set global formatting active flag (g_bFloatingPointFormattingActive = 1)\n2. Call FormatFloatingPointString with provided parameters\n3. Clear global formatting active flag (g_bFloatingPointFormattingActive = 0)\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- dwFormatFlags (uint): Format control flags passed to FormatFloatingPointString\n- lpszOutputBuffer (char *): Target buffer for formatted output string\n- dwBufferSize (size_t): Maximum buffer size for safety bounds checking\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value, output written to lpszOutputBuffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Global flag prevents recursive formatting operations\n- Flag is always cleared even if FormatFloatingPointString fails\n- State tracking allows other functions to detect active formatting\n\nError Handling:\n- No error checking performed at this wrapper level\n- All error handling delegated to FormatFloatingPointString",
