      "name": "ConvertBufferPairsWithLookup",
      "signature": "int ConvertBufferPairsWithLookup(int nElementCount, int nChecksum)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Converts buffer pairs using lookup table expansion for data transformation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter with element count parameter\n2. Read byte from current destination buffer, advance pointer by 1\n3. Look up 16-bit value in global lookup table using byte as index\n4. Write lookup result as both short (2 bytes) and byte (1 byte) to current source buffer\n5. Advance current source buffer pointer by 3 bytes total (2+1)\n6. Read byte from end destination buffer, advance pointer by 1\n7. Look up 16-bit value in global lookup table using byte as index  \n8. Write lookup result as both short (2 bytes) and byte (1 byte) to end source buffer\n9. Advance end source buffer pointer by 3 bytes total (2+1)\n10. Decrement loop counter and repeat until zero\n11. Return sum of original element count and checksum parameters\n\nParameters:\n- nElementCount (int): Number of buffer pairs to process in the conversion loop\n- nChecksum (int): Checksum value added to element count for result calculation\n\nReturns:\n- int: Sum of nElementCount + nChecksum for validation/verification purposes\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Global buffer pointers are modified as side effects during processing\n- Each iteration processes exactly one byte from each destination buffer\n- Each iteration writes exactly 3 bytes to each source buffer (ushort + byte)\n- Lookup table access uses byte value directly as index without bounds checking\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x3 (3): Bytes written per iteration to each source buffer (2-byte short + 1-byte low)\n- Array stride in lookup: [EAX*0x4 + table_base] indicates 4-byte entries (32-bit values)\n\nGlobal Buffer Side Effects:\n- g_pDstBufferCurrent: Advanced by 1 byte per iteration (read source)\n- g_pDstBufferEnd: Advanced by 1 byte per iteration (read source)  \n- g_pSrcBufferCurrent: Advanced by 3 bytes per iteration (write destination)\n- g_pSrcBufferEnd: Advanced by 3 bytes per iteration (write destination)\n\nLookup Table Format:\n- g_anLookupTable: Array of 256 entries, each 4 bytes (likely ushort values)\n- Accessed as: table[(byte_value * 4) + base_address]\n- Returns 16-bit values that are written as both ushort and truncated byte",
