      "comment": "Sets audio volume level for a Bink video handle.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pBinkHandle is not NULL\n2. Check if Bink object is initialized (dwInitStatus != -1)\n3. Verify volume callback function pointer exists (pfnVolumeCallback != NULL)\n4. Call volume callback with audio context pointer and volume level\n\nParameters:\npBinkHandle (BinkObject *): Pointer to Bink video object structure\ndwVolumeLevel (uint): Audio volume level (0-65535 range typical)\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pBinkHandle: Function exits silently\n- Uninitialized Bink object (dwInitStatus == -1): Function exits silently  \n- No volume callback (pfnVolumeCallback == NULL): Function exits silently\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name          | Type    | Description\n-------|------|--------------------|---------|---------------------------------\n0x000  | 488  | reserved1          | byte[]  | Unknown data area\n0x1E8  | 4    | dwInitStatus       | uint    | Initialization status (-1 = uninitialized)\n0x1EC  | 200  | reserved2          | byte[]  | Unknown data area\n0x2A4  | 4    | pAudioContext      | void*   | Audio context passed to callback\n0x2A8  | 12   | reserved3          | byte[]  | Unknown data area  \n0x2B0  | 4    | pfnVolumeCallback  | void*   | Volume callback function pointer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1e8: Offset to dwInitStatus field in BinkObject\n0x2b0: Offset to pfnVolumeCallback field in BinkObject\n0x2a4: Offset to pAudioContext field in BinkObject\n-1: Indicates uninitialized Bink object state",
