      "name": "CleanupFileDescriptorTable",
      "signature": "void CleanupFileDescriptorTable(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Cleanup and deallocate all allocated file descriptors in the global descriptor table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pointer to start of global file descriptor table at 0x1003cce0\n2. Loop through each entry in the descriptor table (64 entries total)\n3. For each entry, check if the descriptor pointer is non-null\n4. If non-null, call SmartFree() to deallocate the descriptor memory\n5. Set the descriptor table entry to null (0x00000000) after deallocation\n6. Advance to next descriptor table entry (+4 bytes)\n7. Continue until reaching end of table at 0x1003cde0\n8. Return after processing all entries\n\nParameters:\nNone - function operates on global data\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, performs cleanup operation only\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNull descriptor entries are skipped without error\nFunction is called during DLL cleanup/finalization\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1003cce0 - Start address of global file descriptor table\n0x1003cde0 - End address of global file descriptor table (exclusive)\n0x00000100 - Size of descriptor table in bytes (256 bytes / 64 entries)\n0x00000004 - Size of each pointer entry in descriptor table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
