      "name": "ReleaseDirectSoundReference",
      "signature": "void ReleaseDirectSoundReference(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Release DirectSound object reference with automatic cleanup on final release.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Decrement global DirectSound reference counter (g_dwDirectSoundReferenceCount)\n2. Check if reference count has reached zero (0)\n3. Verify DirectSound is initialized (g_dwDirectSoundInitialized != 0)\n4. Validate DirectSound instance pointer is not NULL and not invalid (-1)\n5. Call virtual cleanup function at vtable offset +8 through IDirectSoundBase interface\n6. Reset global DirectSound instance pointer to -1 to mark as released\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If reference count > 0, function returns early without cleanup\n- If DirectSound not initialized, function returns early\n- If DirectSound instance is NULL or -1 (invalid), function returns early\n- Magic number -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) used as sentinel value for released/invalid instance\n\nStructure Layout:\nIDirectSoundBase (12 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name  Type      Description\n0x00    4     vtable      void*     Pointer to virtual function table\n0x04    4     refCount    uint      Reference count for object\n0x08    4     cleanup     void*     Cleanup function pointer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xFFFFFFFF (-1) - Sentinel value indicating released or invalid DirectSound instance",
