      "name": "ProcessPixelsWithColorTransform",
      "signature": "void ProcessPixelsWithColorTransform(int nPixelCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Performs MMX-optimized pixel color transformation with rounding and matrix multiplication.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load MMX constants for zero mask, multiplier, and rounding values\n2. Calculate source buffer end address (current + nPixelCount * 3 bytes per pixel)\n3. Enter main processing loop for source buffer range\n4. Load two 32-bit destination pixels and unpack to 16-bit components with zero masking\n5. Apply left shift by 2 bits and high-precision multiply with transform matrix\n6. Add rounding constant and subtract to implement proper rounding\n7. Extract 16-bit components from MMX registers for matrix multiplication\n8. Multiply extracted components with 4x4 transformation matrix from DAT_1002e020\n9. Combine results using bit shifts and pack into 24-bit RGB output format\n10. Store transformed pixels to source buffer and advance pointers\n11. Repeat processing loop for remaining buffer (end buffer processing)\n12. Update global source buffer end pointer\n\nParameters:\nnPixelCount - Number of pixels to process in the transformation\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function modifies global buffer pointers and pixel data in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction processes pixels in pairs for MMX efficiency\nUses saturated arithmetic to prevent overflow during color transformation\nMatrix multiplication coefficients stored as 16-bit signed values at DAT_1002e020\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x02 - Left shift amount for 4x precision in fixed-point arithmetic\n0x18, 0x08, 0x28 - Bit shift amounts for RGB component packing/unpacking\nDAT_1002e020 - 4x4 color transformation matrix (64-bit MMX register format)\n\nStructure Layout:\nNo structure access - operates on packed pixel data and MMX registers\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error checking - assumes valid buffer pointers and pixel count\nRelies on caller to ensure buffer bounds and valid transformation matrix",
