      "name": "ProcessYuvPixelPairs",
      "signature": "int ProcessYuvPixelPairs(int nPixelCount, int nProcessedOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Process YUV pixel pairs with color space conversion and buffer management\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Initialize loop counter with pixel count parameter\n2. Begin pixel pair processing loop:\n   a. Decrement loop counter by 2 (processes 2 pixels per iteration)\n   b. Extract V chroma component from g_pChromaBufferV\n   c. Extract U chroma component from g_pChromaBufferU  \n   d. Load luma data from g_pDstBufferCurrent with offset\n   e. Concatenate V, luma+1, and U components into 32-bit value\n   f. Advance chroma buffer pointers by 1 byte each\n   g. Advance destination buffer current pointer by 2 bytes\n   h. Store concatenated pixel data to g_pSrcBufferCurrent\n3. Process second pixel in pair:\n   a. Load byte from g_pDstBufferEnd + 1 offset\n   b. Load base pixel data from g_pDstBufferEnd\n   c. Advance destination buffer end pointer by 2 bytes\n   d. Combine components with bit shifting: byte<<16 | (concat&0xff00ff)<<8 | base\n   e. Store combined pixel to g_pSrcBufferEnd\n4. Advance source buffer pointers by 4 bytes each\n5. Continue loop while pixel count > 0\n6. Return sum of original pixel count and processed offset\n\nParameters:\n\nnPixelCount (int) - Number of pixel pairs to process\nnProcessedOffset (int) - Processing offset value added to final result\n\nReturns:\n\nSum of nPixelCount and nProcessedOffset indicating total processed count\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x2 - Pixel pair stride for destination buffer advance\n0x1 - Single byte advance for chroma buffers\n0x4 - Source buffer advance (4 bytes per processed pair)\n0x8 - Bit shift amount for concatenation operations\n0x10 - Left shift for high byte positioning  \n0xff00ff - Bit mask to preserve V and U components during combination\n\nGlobal Buffer State Changes:\ng_pChromaBufferV - Advanced by nPixelCount/2 bytes\ng_pChromaBufferU - Advanced by nPixelCount/2 bytes\ng_pDstBufferCurrent - Advanced by nPixelCount bytes\ng_pDstBufferEnd - Advanced by nPixelCount bytes\ng_pSrcBufferCurrent - Advanced by nPixelCount/2 * 4 bytes\ng_pSrcBufferEnd - Advanced by nPixelCount/2 * 4 bytes",
