      "name": "ProcessExtendedPrecisionDivision",
      "signature": "uint ProcessExtendedPrecisionDivision(int nMantissaLow, uint dwMantissaHigh, ushort wExponent, uint dwExtensionBits, uint dwSecondMantissaLow, uint dwSecondExponent)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Processes extended precision floating-point division with denormalization and special value handling\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Construct first extended precision operand from mantissa components and exponent\n2. Check for overflow conditions using CARRY4 flag \n3. Handle special cases: zero operands, infinity, and NaN values\n4. Validate second operand exponent and mantissa for special values\n5. Apply scaling factor from global constant for denormalization\n6. Extract updated mantissa components from scaled result\n7. Process denormalized numbers using XOR mask (0xe000000)\n8. Use lookup table (DAT_1002e960) for exponent range validation\n9. Apply FPU control word manipulation for precision control\n10. Perform conditional multiplication based on second exponent value\n11. Return final division result or error condition code\n\nParameters:\nnMantissaLow (int): Lower 32 bits of first operand mantissa\ndwMantissaHigh (uint): Upper 32 bits of first operand mantissa  \nwExponent (ushort): 15-bit exponent of first operand (IEEE 754 format)\ndwExtensionBits (uint): Extension bits for extended precision format\ndwSecondMantissaLow (uint): Lower 32 bits of second operand mantissa\ndwSecondExponent (uint): Exponent and sign bits of second operand\n\nReturns:\nuint: Division result mantissa or special value\n      0x0000 - Zero result from zero operands\n      0x7FFF - Infinity result from special case handling  \n      exponent & 0x7FFF - Extracted exponent for normal cases\n      mantissa * 2 - Doubled mantissa for carry conditions\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero operands (nMantissaLow == 0 && dwMantissaHigh == 0) return 0x0000\n- Infinity operands (exponent == 0x7FFF) return 0x7FFF\n- Denormalized inputs trigger scaling with constant from 0x1002E978\n- Lookup table DAT_1002E960 validates exponent ranges for special handling\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x7FFF - IEEE 754 extended precision infinity/NaN exponent\n0xE000000 - Denormalization detection mask for mantissa overflow  \n0x1002E960 - Global lookup table for exponent validation\n0x1002E970 - Float constant for conditional multiplication (exponent != 1)\n0x1002E974 - Float constant for conditional multiplication (exponent == 1) \n0x1002E978 - Extended precision scaling constant for denormalization",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:35a926809c02214f1c021da8fe53c5e6",
