      "name": "BinkBufferSetScale",
      "signature": "bool BinkBufferSetScale(uint * pBinkBuffer, uint dwTargetWidth, uint dwTargetHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Sets the display scaling for a Bink video buffer to match target dimensions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input buffer pointer is not NULL, return false if invalid\n2. Use default screen dimensions if target width/height parameters are zero\n3. Compare target width against original buffer width to determine width scaling type:\n   - If target is multiple of original: Set upscale flag (0x80000000)\n   - If original is multiple of target: Set downscale flag (0x20000000)  \n   - If target > original: Set enlarge flag (0x40000000)\n   - If target < original: Set shrink flag (0x10000000)\n4. Check if buffer supports the calculated width scaling type via flags at offset 0x38\n5. If width scaling supported, store target width at buffer offset 0x3C\n6. Repeat steps 3-5 for height scaling with different flag values:\n   - Upscale: 0x8000000, Downscale: 0x2000000, Enlarge: 0x4000000, Shrink: 0x1000000\n7. Store target height at buffer offset 0x40 if height scaling supported\n8. Calculate final display coordinates by adding offsets to scaled dimensions\n9. Return true only if both width and height scaling are supported\n\nParameters:\npBinkBuffer (uint *): Pointer to BinkBuffer structure containing video data and scaling configuration\ndwTargetWidth (uint): Desired display width in pixels, 0 uses screen width default\ndwTargetHeight (uint): Desired display height in pixels, 0 uses screen height default\n\nReturns:\nbool: True if both width and height scaling are supported by buffer capabilities, false otherwise\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x80000000 - Width upscale flag (target is multiple of original width)\n0x20000000 - Width downscale flag (original is multiple of target width)\n0x40000000 - Width enlarge flag (target width > original width)\n0x10000000 - Width shrink flag (target width < original width)\n0x8000000 - Height upscale flag (target is multiple of original height)\n0x2000000 - Height downscale flag (original is multiple of target height)  \n0x4000000 - Height enlarge flag (target height > original height)\n0x1000000 - Height shrink flag (target height < original height)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type   Description\n0x00    4     originalWidth        uint   Original video frame width\n0x04    4     originalHeight       uint   Original video frame height\n0x08    4     displayX             uint   Final X coordinate for display\n0x0C    4     displayY             uint   Final Y coordinate for display\n0x30    4     xOffset              uint   X offset for positioning\n0x34    4     yOffset              uint   Y offset for positioning  \n0x38    4     scalingCapabilities  uint   Bitfield of supported scaling modes\n0x3C    4     scaledWidth          uint   Calculated scaled width\n0x40    4     scaledHeight         uint   Calculated scaled height",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
