      "name": "ConvertYuvToRgbWithMmx",
      "signature": "void ConvertYuvToRgbWithMmx(dword nScanlineWidth)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Convert YUV color space to RGB using MMX SIMD instructions for two scanlines.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize global buffer pointers and MMX rounding constant (0x1002dfc8)\n2. Process current scanline pixels in main loop:\n   a. Load source ARGB pixel from destination buffer\n   b. Extract chroma U and V components from respective buffers\n   c. Unpack pixel bytes to 16-bit words for MMX processing\n   d. Subtract zero mask (0x1002dfb8) and multiply by 2 for precision scaling\n   e. Multiply by MMX multiplier constant (0x1002dfc0) for color space conversion\n   f. Add values from Red, Green, Blue, and Green Chroma lookup tables\n   g. Apply rounding constant and perform saturation arithmetic\n   h. Right shift by component-specific amounts, then left shift for final positioning\n   i. Combine RGB channels using bitwise OR operations\n   j. Write final RGB values back to destination buffer with pixel duplication\n3. Update global buffer pointers by scanline width * 4 bytes per pixel\n4. Process end scanline pixels using identical logic with different buffer sets\n5. Restore global buffer states and return\n\nParameters:\nnScanlineWidth - Width of scanline in pixels to process\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, results written directly to global buffers\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1002dfc8 - MMX rounding constant for color space conversion\n0x1002dfb8 - MMX zero mask for unsigned byte subtraction\n0x1002dfc0 - MMX multiplier constant for YUV scaling\n0x10034f30 - Red component lookup table base address\n0x10034730 - Red lookup table base address \n0x10034b30 - Blue component lookup table base address\n0x10035330 - Green chroma lookup table base address\n0x1003c7f0 - Red channel right shift amount (global)\n0x1003c7d8 - Red channel left shift amount (global)  \n0x1003c7f8 - Green channel right shift amount (global)\n0x1003c7e0 - Green channel left shift amount (global)\n0x1003c800 - Blue channel right shift amount (global)\n0x1003c7e8 - Blue channel left shift amount (global)\n\nGlobal Buffers:\ng_pSrcBufferCurrent (0x100332e0) - Current scanline source buffer pointer\ng_pSrcBufferEnd (0x100332e4) - End scanline source buffer pointer  \ng_pDstBufferCurrent (0x100332e8) - Current scanline destination pointer\ng_pDstBufferEnd (0x100332ec) - End scanline destination pointer\ng_pChromaBufferU (0x100332f0) - U chroma component buffer pointer\ng_pChromaBufferV (0x100332f4) - V chroma component buffer pointer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function processes exactly two scanlines using identical conversion logic\n- MMX registers maintain 64-bit parallel processing for 4 pixels simultaneously\n- Chroma buffers advance by 2 bytes per iteration (U and V interleaved)\n- Destination pixels are duplicated during final write operations\n- All pointer arithmetic performed in 4-byte increments for 32-bit pixels",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
