      "name": "BlendPixelBuffersWithMmx",
      "signature": "void BlendPixelBuffersWithMmx(int nPixelCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Performs MMX-optimized pixel blending between two RGBA buffer streams using packed byte operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load 64-bit MMX blend mask (0x8080808080808080) for alpha blending operations\n2. Calculate end pointer by advancing source buffer by nPixelCount * 4 dwords (16 bytes per iteration)\n3. Enter main processing loop with dual buffer operations:\n   a. Load 32-bit pixel from destination end buffer, extract RGBA bytes\n   b. Load 32-bit pixel from destination current buffer, extract RGBA bytes\n   c. Duplicate pixel bytes using PUNPCKLBW for 16-bit channel expansion\n   d. Perform packed byte blending with MMX mask\n   e. Store 2 qwords (16 bytes) to source end buffer with blended results\n   f. Store 2 qwords (16 bytes) to source current buffer with blended results\n   g. Advance all pointers: dst buffers +4 bytes, src buffers +16 bytes\n4. Continue until source current pointer reaches calculated end boundary\n5. Update global buffer pointers with final positions\n\nParameters:\nnPixelCount: Number of 32-bit pixels to process (determines loop iterations)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic Number 0x8080808080808080: MMX alpha blend mask for packed byte operations\nMagic Number 0x4: Dword size multiplier for pixel count to byte offset conversion\nMagic Number 0x10: 16-byte stride per iteration (4 pixels * 4 bytes each)\n\nMMX Operations:\nPUNPCKLBW: Unpack low bytes with zero interleaving for 16-bit precision\nPUNPCKHBW: Unpack high bytes with zero interleaving for 16-bit precision\nMOVQ: 64-bit MMX register transfer for packed pixel data",
