      "name": "FftRadix2DecimationInTime",
      "signature": "void FftRadix2DecimationInTime(int nSize, float * pComplexData, FftParams * pParams)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Performs Fast Fourier Transform using radix-2 decimation-in-time algorithm with optimized butterfly operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input size and determine initial stride (minimum 2)\n2. If size > 16 (0x10), call ProcessFftRadix2Butterfly for initial stage\n3. If size > 128 (0x80), perform iterative radix-2 butterfly operations\n   - Start with stride 128, multiply by 8 each iteration\n   - Continue until stride * 8 >= input size\n4. Perform final butterfly stage based on remaining size:\n   - If stride * 4 < size: 8-point radix-2 butterfly with twiddle factors\n   - If stride * 4 == size: 4-point radix-2 butterfly (no twiddles)\n   - Otherwise: 2-point radix-2 butterfly (simple addition/subtraction)\n5. Update complex data array in-place with transformed values\n\nParameters:\nnSize: Size of the FFT (must be power of 2, minimum 2)\npComplexData: Array of interleaved complex numbers (real, imag, real, imag...)\npParams: FFT parameters structure containing twiddle factor at offset +8\n\nReturns:\nvoid (modifies pComplexData in-place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Size <= 16: Only performs final butterfly stage\n- Size <= 128: Skips iterative multiplication stage  \n- Twiddle factor multiplication only applied in 8-point butterfly stage\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10 (16): Threshold for ProcessFftRadix2Butterfly call\n0x80 (128): Threshold for iterative radix-2 butterfly loop\n0x8 (8): Stride multiplier for each iteration\n0x4 (4): Final stage stride multiplier for 8-point butterfly\n0x2 (2): Minimum initial stride value\n\nStructure Layout:\nFftParams (12 bytes total):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type  | Description\n0x00   | 4    | reserved1     | uint  | Reserved field 1\n0x04   | 4    | reserved2     | uint  | Reserved field 2  \n0x08   | 4    | twiddleFactor | float | Twiddle factor for complex multiplication",
