      "name": "FindAndCacheMainWindow",
      "signature": "void FindAndCacheMainWindow(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Find and cache the main window handle for the current process.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current process ID using GetCurrentProcessId API\n2. Get current module handle using GetModuleHandleA API  \n3. Check if global window cache (g_pMainWindow) is already populated\n4. If cached window exists, return immediately (early exit)\n5. Begin window enumeration using GetTopWindow with NULL desktop\n6. For each top-level window found:\n   - Get window's owning process ID via GetWindowThreadProcessId\n   - Compare against current process ID for ownership match\n   - If owned by current process, get window's module handle via GetWindowLongA(-6)\n   - Compare window module against current process module\n   - Get window style flags via GetWindowLongA(-16) \n   - Check if WS_CHILD flag (0x40000000) is clear (top-level window)\n   - If module matches AND not child window, cache as main window\n   - If no perfect match, cache any window from current process as fallback\n7. Continue enumeration via GetWindow with GW_HWNDNEXT (2) flag\n8. If no windows found after enumeration, get active window as final fallback\n9. Store result in global cache variable g_pMainWindow\n\nParameters:\n(none - void function)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Result stored in global g_pMainWindow variable\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if g_pMainWindow already cached (optimization)\n- Fallback to any process window if no perfect module/style match found\n- Final fallback to GetActiveWindow if no process windows exist\n- Window module comparison prevents matching windows from loaded DLLs\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x40000000 - WS_CHILD window style flag (indicates child window)\n-6 - GWL_HINSTANCE offset for GetWindowLongA (window's module handle)\n-16 - GWL_STYLE offset for GetWindowLongA (window style flags)  \n2 - GW_HWNDNEXT flag for GetWindow (next sibling window)\n\nError Handling:\n- NULL handle returns from GetTopWindow indicate no top-level windows\n- GetWindowThreadProcessId failure leaves dwThreadProcessId unchanged\n- GetWindowLongA returns 0 for invalid windows (handled by comparison logic)\n- GetActiveWindow may return NULL if no active window exists",
