      "name": "StopAudioPlayback",
      "signature": "int StopAudioPlayback(AudioContext * pAudioContext, int nBufferPosition)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Stops audio playback and clears the associated buffer with silence patterns.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate audio context has active buffer (offset 0x6c != -1)\n2. Validate buffer pointer exists (offset 0x78 != 0)  \n3. Calculate bytes to clear from buffer size minus position\n4. Determine silence byte pattern based on audio format (0x80 for 16-bit, 0x00 for other)\n5. Fill buffer with silence using optimized DWORD writes for bulk data\n6. Fill remaining bytes individually for partial DWORD alignment\n7. Invoke audio virtual method to notify audio system of stop\n8. Clear buffer tracking fields (0x6c = -1, 0x78 = 0)\n9. Return success status\n\nParameters:\npAudioContext - Pointer to AudioContext structure containing buffer state\nnBufferPosition - Current position in audio buffer (bytes from start)\n\nReturns:\n1 - Successfully stopped playback and cleared buffer\n0 - No active buffer or invalid context\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf audio format at offset 0x50 equals 0x10 (16-bit), uses 0x80 silence byte\nOtherwise uses 0x00 silence byte for 8-bit formats\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6c - Audio buffer state flag (-1 = inactive, other = active)\n0x78 - Audio buffer pointer (0 = no buffer)\n0x74 - Audio buffer size in bytes  \n0x50 - Audio format flags (0x10 = 16-bit format)\n0x3c - AudioCallParams structure offset for virtual method calls\n0x80808080 - 32-bit silence pattern for 16-bit audio\n0x80 - Single byte silence value for 16-bit audio\n-1 (0xffffffff) - Inactive buffer state marker\n\nStructure Layout:\nAudioContext Structure:\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type | Description  \n0x3c   | 60   | callParams    | byte[60] | Virtual method call parameters\n0x50   | 4    | formatFlags   | uint | Audio format configuration (0x10 = 16-bit)\n0x6c   | 4    | bufferState   | int  | Buffer state (-1 = inactive, other = active)  \n0x74   | 4    | bufferSize    | uint | Total buffer size in bytes\n0x78   | 4    | bufferPtr     | void*| Pointer to audio buffer memory",
