      "name": "BinkSetSoundOnOff",
      "signature": "int BinkSetSoundOnOff(BinkInstance * pBinkInstance, int nSoundEnabled)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Controls audio playback state for Bink video instances with thread-safe locking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate Bink instance pointer (non-null, valid state flag at +0x1E8 != -1)\n2. Verify audio callback function pointer exists at +0x2BC (offset 700)\n3. Call audio subsystem callback at +0x2A4 with sound enable/disable flag\n4. Handle disable sound request (callback returns 0, currently enabled):\n   a. Acquire thread lock at +0x29C using atomic increment\n   b. Wait for exclusive access (lock counter == 1) with Sleep(0) yield\n   c. Reset audio buffer pointers: copy +0x284 to +0x28C and +0x290\n   d. Clear buffer usage counter at +0x298 to 0\n   e. Set sound enabled state at +0x22C to 0 (disabled)\n   f. Release lock using atomic decrement\n5. Handle enable sound request (callback returns 1, currently disabled):\n   a. Acquire thread lock at +0x29C using atomic increment  \n   b. Wait for exclusive access (lock counter == 1) with Sleep(0) yield\n   c. Check audio format conditions at +0xC (not 1 and not equal to +0xEC)\n   d. If buffer clear needed: get buffer size from +0x370, zero buffer at +0x284\n      - Clear by DWORDs first (size >> 2 iterations), then remaining bytes\n      - Update buffer end pointer (+0x28C = +0x284 + size) and reset pointer (+0x290)\n   e. Set sound enabled state at +0x22C to 1 (enabled) \n   f. Clear audio state flag at +0x20C to 0\n   g. Release lock using atomic decrement\n6. Return audio subsystem result code\n\nParameters:\npBinkInstance - Pointer to Bink video instance structure containing audio state\nnSoundEnabled - Audio enable flag: 1 to enable sound, 0 to disable sound\nIMPLICIT - Uses Sleep() API for cooperative multitasking during lock waits\n\nReturns:\n0 - Success (sound state changed successfully)\n1 - Success (sound state set successfully) \nOther - Audio subsystem error code from callback function\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic Numbers: 0x1E8 (488) = instance validity flag offset, 0x2BC (700) = callback pointer offset, 0x2A4 (676) = callback data offset, 0x22C (556) = sound enabled state offset, 0x29C (668) = thread lock counter offset, 0x284 (644) = audio buffer base pointer, 0x28C (652) = buffer end pointer, 0x290 (656) = current buffer pointer, 0x298 (664) = buffer usage counter, 0xC (12) = audio format type, 0xEC (236) = reference format, 0x370 (880) = buffer size, 0x20C (524) = audio state flag\n\nError Handling:\n- Returns unchanged result if Bink instance invalid or no audio callback\n- Uses atomic operations (LOCK prefix) for thread-safe lock management\n- Cooperative multitasking with Sleep(0) prevents busy-wait deadlock\n- Early exit paths preserve original error codes from audio subsystem",
