      "name": "DecodeLiteralBytesFromBitstream",
      "signature": "void DecodeLiteralBytesFromBitstream(int * pDecoderContext, int * pBitStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Decodes literal bytes from a compressed bitstream using variable-length encoding\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if output buffer has space (current pointer == end pointer)\n2. Read variable-length count from input bitstream using bit manipulation\n3. If count is 0, advance output pointers by 4 bytes and return\n4. Initialize output buffer pointers using decoder context buffer\n5. Read compression flag bit from bitstream\n6. If flag is 0 (literal mode):\n   a. For each byte to decode:\n      - Extract bit count from decoder tables\n      - Read encoded byte from lookup table using bit pattern\n      - Decode byte using lookup table at decoder context + 0x10\n      - Store decoded byte to output buffer\n      - Update bit accumulator and position\n7. If flag is 1 (run-length mode):\n   a. Read 4-bit fill value from bitstream\n   b. Write fill value to output buffer for count bytes\n   c. Use optimized 32-bit writes for multiples of 4 bytes\n8. Update input bitstream state (data pointer, accumulator, bit position)\n\nParameters:\npDecoderContext (BitstreamContext *): Decoder state containing output buffers,\n    bit count tables, and lookup tables. Uses fields at offsets 0x0-0x4 (output \n    range), 0x10 (decode table), 0x20-0x24 (bit count tables), 0x28 (bit count),\n    and 0x2c (buffer pointer).\npBitStream (BitStream *): Input bitstream state with data pointer at 0x0,\n    saved field at 0x4, bit accumulator at 0x8, and available bits at 0xc\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates both decoder context and bitstream structures in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf decoded count is 0, function advances output pointers without decoding data\nRun-length mode uses 4-bit fill values replicated to all bytes\nBit extraction uses complex shifting to handle cross-word boundaries\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1f (31) - Maximum bit shift count for 32-bit operations\n0xf (15) - 4-bit mask for nibble extraction and fill values  \n0x10 (16) - Offset to decode lookup table in decoder context\n0x20 (32) - Size of machine word for bit operations\n0xf0f0f0f - Replicated nibble pattern for run-length fills\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error checking - assumes valid input and sufficient buffer space\nBitstream exhaustion handled by reading next word automatically\nInvalid bit counts may cause incorrect decoding or buffer overrun",
