      "name": "TransformBufferWithLookupTable",
      "signature": "int TransformBufferWithLookupTable(int nIterationCount, int nOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Transforms buffer data using a lookup table for both current and end buffer positions\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter with iteration count parameter\n2. Read byte from current destination buffer position and advance pointer\n3. Transform byte using lookup table: value = table[byte] | (table[byte] << 8)\n4. Write transformed value as DWORD to current source buffer position\n5. Write transformed value as WORD to source buffer position + 4\n6. Read byte from end destination buffer position and advance pointer  \n7. Transform byte using same lookup table operation\n8. Write transformed value as DWORD to end source buffer position\n9. Write transformed value as WORD to end source buffer position + 4\n10. Advance both source buffer pointers by 6 bytes (4-byte DWORD + 2-byte WORD)\n11. Decrement loop counter and repeat until zero\n12. Return sum of iteration count and offset parameters\n\nParameters:\n  nIterationCount (int) - Number of buffer transformation iterations to perform\n  nOffset (int) - Offset value to add to iteration count in return value\n\nReturns:\n  int - Sum of nIterationCount + nOffset (processing confirmation value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  If nIterationCount is 0, function returns immediately with just nOffset\n  Lookup table entries are duplicated (value | value << 8) to create 16-bit patterns\n  Buffer advancement is fixed at 6 bytes per iteration regardless of data size\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x6 (6) - Buffer advancement stride (4-byte DWORD + 2-byte WORD)\n  0x8 (8) - Left shift amount for creating 16-bit pattern from lookup value\n  0x4 (4) - Offset for WORD write after DWORD write\n\nError Handling:\n  No bounds checking on buffer pointers - assumes caller validates buffer sizes\n  No validation of lookup table entries - assumes table is properly initialized\n  Loop counter decrements without overflow protection - relies on positive input",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
