      "name": "ComputeExtendedPrecisionLogarithm",
      "signature": "float10 ComputeExtendedPrecisionLogarithm(float10 * __return_storage_ptr__, int nOperation, uint dwFlags, int nPrecision, uint dwOptions)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "float10 *",
      "comment": "Computes extended precision logarithm with comprehensive error handling and edge case support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store FPU control word and check if it matches expected value (0x27f)\n2. If control word incorrect, call FPU initialization routine (FUN_1001edd5)\n3. Extract exponent field (bits 20-30) from input parameter and check for infinity\n4. If exponent equals 0x7ff00000 (infinity), branch to special infinity handling\n5. Call floating point validation routine (FUN_1001ee05) to check for NaN/infinity\n6. If validation fails, return zero and set error flag\n7. Check if input is zero by testing mantissa and exponent fields\n8. If input is zero, handle special zero case with sign bit processing\n9. Extract sign bit from high byte of parameter and check for negative values\n10. If negative input detected, branch to complex logarithm error handling\n11. Compute y*log2(x) using FYL2X FPU instruction for core logarithm calculation\n12. Call exponential conversion routine (FUN_1001edc0) to complete calculation\n13. Check and apply sign correction based on original input sign\n14. Handle overflow/underflow conditions by checking math error flag\n15. If math error detected, load appropriate constant (infinity or NaN) and return error code\n16. For successful calculation, return computed extended precision result\n\nParameters:\nnOperation (int) - Operation type selector (0=natural log, 1=base-10, 7=base-2)\ndwFlags (uint) - Computation flags controlling precision and rounding mode\nnPrecision (int) - Precision specification for extended precision calculation\ndwOptions (uint) - Additional options controlling error handling behavior\n\nReturns:\nfloat10 - Extended precision logarithm result (10-byte IEEE extended precision format)\nReturn codes stored in EAX: 0=success, 1=infinity result, 2=underflow, 7=overflow\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Input of +infinity returns +infinity with code 1\n- Input of -infinity returns NaN with error code\n- Input of +0 returns -infinity with code 2  \n- Input of -0 returns -infinity with sign handling\n- Input of NaN returns NaN with error propagation\n- Negative finite inputs return NaN with error code 7\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x27f - Expected FPU control word value for proper rounding\n0x7ff00000 - IEEE double infinity/NaN exponent mask\n0xfffff - IEEE double mantissa extraction mask\n0x80 - Sign bit mask for floating point values\n\nError Handling:\n- Math error flag (g_dwMathErrorFlag) checked for overflow/underflow conditions\n- Error message string (g_szMathErrorMessage) used for diagnostic output\n- Special constant values loaded for infinity (g_ldPositiveInfinity) and NaN (g_ldNaN)\n- FPU state preservation using FSAVE/FRSTOR during external function calls\n\nState Machine:\nState 1: FPU Control Check - Validate FPU control word, initialize if needed\nState 2: Input Classification - Check for infinity, NaN, zero, negative values  \nState 3: Core Calculation - Use FYL2X instruction for logarithm computation\nState 4: Result Processing - Apply sign correction and handle special cases\nState 5: Error Handling - Load error constants and set appropriate return codes\n\nNote: Function uses 5 stack-allocated temporary variables optimized away by decompiler:\n- local_4 (undefined2): FPU control word storage at [ESP-0x4]\n- local_70 (undefined1[10]): Extended precision temporary at [ESP-0x70] \n- local_78 (undefined8): Double precision temporary at [ESP-0x78]\n- local_84 (undefined8): Double precision temporary at [ESP-0x84]\n- local_8c (undefined8): Double precision temporary at [ESP-0x8c]",
