      "name": "BinkCheckCursor",
      "signature": "int BinkCheckCursor(HWND hWnd, int nLeft, int nTop, int nWidth, int nHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Checks if cursor is within specified rectangle and hides cursor if inside bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize cursor tolerance values if not already set (SM_CXDOUBLECLK and SM_CYDOUBLECLK)\n2. Convert client coordinates (nLeft, nTop) to screen coordinates using ClientToScreen\n3. Get current cursor position using GetCursorPos\n4. Check if cursor is within tolerance-adjusted rectangle bounds\n5. If cursor is inside bounds, repeatedly call ShowCursor(0) until cursor is hidden\n6. Return count of ShowCursor calls made\n\nParameters:\nhWnd - Window handle for coordinate conversion (NULL = use screen coordinates)\nnLeft - Left boundary of rectangle in client coordinates\nnTop - Top boundary of rectangle in client coordinates  \nnWidth - Width of rectangle in pixels\nnHeight - Height of rectangle in pixels\n\nReturns:\nCount of ShowCursor(0) calls made (cursor hide operations performed)\n0 if cursor was outside bounds or already hidden\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf hWnd is NULL, coordinates are treated as screen coordinates\nCursor tolerance values (g_nCursorToleranceX, g_nCursorToleranceY) are cached globally\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xd (13) - SM_CXDOUBLECLK system metric for X cursor tolerance\n0xe (14) - SM_CYDOUBLECLK system metric for Y cursor tolerance\n0 - ShowCursor parameter to hide cursor\n-1 - ShowCursor return threshold (cursor visible when >= 0)",
