      "name": "ConvertFloatToFormatState",
      "signature": "void * ConvertFloatToFormatState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Converts floating-point value from stack to formatted string representation and populates global format state structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract 32-bit floating-point value from stack parameter at offset ffffffd8\n2. Decompose value into high and low 16-bit words using bit shift operations\n3. Call FUN_1002035b to convert float to extended precision format (10-byte float)\n4. Call FUN_10022459 to format extended float as decimal string with precision 0x11\n5. Populate global FloatFormatState structure with formatting results\n6. Set sign character from formatted result at g_bSignChar\n7. Set formatted value from buffer start at g_wFormatBuffer\n8. Set pointer to digit buffer at g_szDigitBuffer\n9. Return pointer to populated global format state structure\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT dwFloatValue: 32-bit floating-point value passed on stack (IEEE 754 format)\n\nReturns:\nPointer to global FloatFormatState structure containing:\n- Sign character (space or minus)\n- Formatted integer portion\n- Pointer to digit string buffer\n- Result status code from formatting operation\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0x11 (17 decimal): Precision parameter for decimal formatting\nStack offset ffffffd8: Negative stack offset indicating parameter above return address\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type    Description\n0x00    4     nResult      int     Formatting result code from FUN_10022459\n0x04    4     nSign        int     Sign character converted to integer\n0x08    4     pBuffer      char*   Pointer to formatted digit buffer\n0x0C    4     dwStatus     uint    Status flags from formatting operation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:5a025588439cc101ffb982cfa5323a2c",
