      "name": "WaitForDirectSoundBufferReady",
      "signature": "void WaitForDirectSoundBufferReady(DirectSoundContext * pDsContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Waits for DirectSound buffer to become ready by polling until buffer lost error is resolved\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter polling loop to check DirectSound buffer status\n2. Call virtual function at offset 0x30 (likely IDirectSoundBuffer::GetStatus or Lock)\n3. Check if return value is DSERR_BUFFERLOST (0x88780096)\n4. If buffer lost: Sleep for 10ms to avoid busy waiting\n5. Call virtual function at offset 0x50 (likely IDirectSoundBuffer::Restore)\n6. Continue polling until buffer is available\n7. Clear audio configuration fields to reset state\n\nParameters:\npDsContext - Pointer to DirectSoundContext structure containing buffer interface\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nBusy polling loop with sleep prevents excessive CPU usage during buffer recovery\nFunction only exits when buffer becomes available (no timeout)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x88780096 (DSERR_BUFFERLOST) - DirectSound buffer lost error code\n0x30 - Virtual function table offset for status/lock operation\n0x50 - Virtual function table offset for restore operation  \n10 - Sleep duration in milliseconds\n0x34 (0xd * 4) - Offset to wBitsPerSample field\n0x36 (0xd * 4 + 2) - Offset to wChannels field\n\nStructure Layout:\nDirectSoundContext fields accessed:\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type    | Description\n0x00   | 4    | pfnCallback0    | void*   | Pointer to DirectSound buffer interface\n0x34   | 2    | wBitsPerSample  | ushort  | Audio bits per sample (cleared on exit)\n0x36   | 2    | wChannels       | ushort  | Audio channel count (cleared on exit)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
