      "name": "YuvBlitYv12",
      "signature": "void YuvBlitYv12(byte * pDstBuffer, dword nDstX, dword nDstY, dword nDstPitch, byte * pYSrc, byte * pUVSrc, dword nSrcX, dword nSrcY, dword nWidth, dword nHeight, dword nSrcPitch, int nUVHeight, dword dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Performs YUV planar to RGB buffer conversion and blitting for YV12 format video frames.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate and align source/destination coordinates to even boundaries for proper chroma sampling\n2. Adjust width and height to even values to maintain 4:2:0 chroma subsampling alignment\n3. Calculate source and destination pointers for Y plane data transfer\n4. Copy Y (luminance) plane data using optimized DWORD+byte copy loops\n5. Calculate UV plane offsets based on flags (0x10000 = packed layout vs planar layout)\n6. Process U plane: either copy from source or fill with neutral gray (0x80) if flag 0x20000 set\n7. Calculate V plane offset accounting for U plane size and layout format\n8. Process V plane: either copy from source or fill with neutral gray (0x80) if flag 0x20000 set\n\nParameters:\npDstBuffer: Destination RGB buffer base address\nnDstX: Destination X coordinate in pixels\nnDstY: Destination Y coordinate in pixels  \nnDstPitch: Destination buffer row stride in bytes\npYSrc: Source Y plane buffer base address\npUVSrc: Source UV plane buffer base address (interleaved or planar)\nnSrcX: Source X coordinate in pixels\nnSrcY: Source Y coordinate in pixels\nnWidth: Copy width in pixels\nnHeight: Copy height in pixels\nnSrcPitch: Source buffer row stride in bytes\nnUVHeight: Height of UV plane data in lines\ndwFlags: Control flags (0x10000=packed UV layout, 0x20000=fill gray instead of copy)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, performs in-place buffer operations\n\nSpecial Cases:\nHandles odd coordinates by incrementing to next even boundary\nReduces dimensions by 1 when alignment padding applied\nUses 4:2:0 subsampling (UV planes are half resolution of Y)\nGray fill mode (0x80) represents neutral chroma for YUV color space\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10000 - Packed UV layout flag (vs separate U/V planes)\n0x20000 - Fill neutral gray flag (0x80808080 for DWORD, 0x80 for bytes)\n0x80 - Neutral chroma value in YUV color space (128 decimal)\n0x80808080 - 4-pixel neutral chroma fill pattern",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
