      "name": "BinkSetAudioVolume",
      "signature": "void BinkSetAudioVolume(BinkAudioProcessor * pAudioProcessor, uint dwVolumeLevel)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets the audio volume level for a Bink audio processor with linear scaling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input volume level against maximum limit (0x7fff = 32767)\n2. Clamp volume level to maximum if it exceeds the limit\n3. Calculate scaled volume using linear interpolation: (dwVolumeLevel * 0x7f) / 0x7fff\n4. Store the scaled volume in the processor's volume field at offset 0x58\n5. Invoke the audio volume callback function with processor handle and scaled volume\n\nParameters:\npAudioProcessor - Pointer to BinkAudioProcessor structure containing audio context\ndwVolumeLevel - Raw volume level (0 to 0x7fff), values above 0x7fff are clamped\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nVolume levels above 0x7fff (32767) are automatically clamped to prevent overflow\nThe scaling formula produces values from 0 to 0x7f (127) for the full input range\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x7fff (32767) - Maximum allowed volume level input\n0x7f (127) - Maximum scaled volume output value\n0x58 (88) - Offset to volume field in BinkAudioProcessor structure\n0x44 (68) - Offset to audio handle field in BinkAudioProcessor structure\n\nStructure Layout:\nBinkAudioProcessor relevant fields:\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type    Description\n+0x44   4     audioHandle   uint    Handle passed to volume callback\n+0x58   4     volumeLevel   uint    Current scaled volume level (0-127)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
