      "name": "AllocateAndSetupMemoryPointers",
      "signature": "void AllocateAndSetupMemoryPointers(AllocContext * pAllocContext, uint dwSizeBytes)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Allocates aligned memory and sets up tracking pointer arrays for memory management\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate 16-byte aligned allocation size (dwSizeBytes + 0x0F) & 0xFFFFFFF0\n2. Update allocation context's total size tracker at offset 0x234\n3. Allocate memory using RadMalloc with current memory offset plus aligned size\n4. Reset global memory offset tracker to 0\n5. If allocation successful, setup pointer arrays for tracking\n6. Calculate pointer base address by adding aligned size to allocated memory\n7. Iterate through allocation count and populate tracking arrays\n8. Set allocation handle pointers in g_apAllocationHandles[i] to memory addresses\n9. Advance memory pointer by allocation size from g_anAllocationSizes[i]\n10. Reset allocation count tracker to 0\n\nParameters:\npAllocContext (AllocContext*): Pointer to allocation context structure with size tracker at offset 0x234\ndwSizeBytes (uint): Requested allocation size in bytes, will be 16-byte aligned\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0F (15): Alignment mask for 16-byte boundary calculation\n0xFFFFFFF0: Bit mask to clear low 4 bits for 16-byte alignment  \n0x234 (564): Offset to total size tracker field in allocation context structure\n\nGlobal Variables:\ng_dwMemoryOffset (0x1002f668): Current memory offset tracker for allocations\ng_dwAllocationCount (0x1002f66c): Number of tracked memory allocations\ng_apAllocationHandles (0x1002f364): Array of pointers to allocation handles\ng_anAllocationSizes (0x1002f164): Array of allocation sizes for each handle\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf RadMalloc fails (returns NULL), function exits early without setting up pointer arrays\nIf allocation count is 0, skips pointer array setup loop\nMemory offset tracker is always reset to 0 after allocation attempt",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
