      "name": "ConvertYuv422ToRgb24Scanlines",
      "signature": "void ConvertYuv422ToRgb24Scanlines(int nWidth)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts YUV422 to RGB24 scanlines using SIMD optimizations for both current and end line buffers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize chroma buffer pointers (U and V) and source RGB buffer\n2. Calculate source buffer end position (nWidth * 3 bytes per pixel)\n3. Process current scanline loop:\n   a. Extract ARGB pixel and separate into RGB components\n   b. Load chroma U and V values with byte alignment adjustment\n   c. Subtract bias (0x0080) from RGB using PSUBUSW to prevent underflow\n   d. Left shift by 2 and multiply by conversion constants using PMULHW\n   e. Extract 4 luma components (sLuma0-3) from 64-bit SIMD result\n   f. Look up Y-to-RGB conversion values from tables at offsets:\n      - DAT_10034730: Y-to-R conversion table\n      - DAT_10034b30: Y-to-G conversion table (blue component)\n      - DAT_10034f30: Y-to-G conversion table (red component)\n      - DAT_10035330: Y-to-B conversion table\n   g. Add bias vector, clamp with saturation, and pack RGB components\n   h. Store 3 bytes (24-bit RGB) to destination buffer and advance by 3\n   i. Continue until source buffer end reached\n4. Repeat identical process for end scanline buffer\n5. Update global buffer end positions for next frame\n\nParameters:\nnWidth: Width of scanline in pixels (used to calculate buffer stride)\n\nReturns:\nNone (void function modifies global buffer pointers)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nChroma subsampling: U and V advance by 2 bytes while RGB advances by 1\nSIMD saturation: PSUBUSW prevents underflow, PADDSW handles overflow\nBuffer alignment: Byte extraction handles unaligned chroma access\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0080 (128): YUV bias offset for unsigned to signed conversion\n0x18 (24): Right shift for alpha channel extraction\n0x10 (16): Right shift for red channel extraction  \n0x08 (8): Right shift for green channel extraction\n0x02: Left shift multiplier for luma precision\n0x30 (48): 64-bit quad-word high portion shift\n0x20 (32): 64-bit quad-word mid-high shift\n0x1002dfc8: SIMD bias vector constant (4x 0x0080)\n0x1002dfb8: RGB extraction mask (0x00ff00ff pattern)\n0x1002dfc0: Luma multiplication constants\n\nError Handling:\nHardware SIMD saturation prevents arithmetic overflow/underflow\nNo bounds checking - assumes valid buffer pointers from caller\n\nLookup Tables:\nDAT_10034730[256]: Y-to-R conversion coefficients (16.16 fixed point)\nDAT_10034b30[256]: Y-to-G blue component coefficients  \nDAT_10034f30[256]: Y-to-G red component coefficients\nDAT_10035330[256]: Y-to-B conversion coefficients",
