      "name": "MeasureExecutionTime",
      "signature": "void MeasureExecutionTime(uint dwParameter)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Performance measurement wrapper that times callback function execution using CPU timestamps.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Capture current CPU timestamp using RDTSC instruction\n2. Execute callback function via global function pointer, passing through parameter\n3. Capture second CPU timestamp after callback completes\n4. Calculate elapsed time in CPU cycles (end - start)\n5. Pass elapsed time to state machine dispatch function for processing\n\nParameters:\ndwParameter (uint): Parameter to pass through to the callback function unchanged\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- RDTSC instruction returns 64-bit timestamp in EDX:EAX register pair\n- Time calculation truncates to 32-bit for compatibility with dispatch function\n- Function pointer must be valid or system will crash on indirect call\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1000ced0 - ConfigureStateMachineDispatch function address\nRDTSC - Read Time-Stamp Counter x86 instruction for high-precision timing",
