      "name": "FindMaxDifferenceInRange",
      "signature": "uint FindMaxDifferenceInRange(uint dwEndIndex, int * panArray, uint dwStartIndex, int * pnMaxDiffIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Finds the maximum difference between consecutive elements in a specified array range.\nUsed by Bink video codec for analyzing frame size variations and buffer calculations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input range by checking dwEndIndex > dwStartIndex\n2. Initialize tracking variables for maximum difference and index position\n3. Loop through array range from dwStartIndex to dwEndIndex-1\n4. For each position, calculate difference between array[i+offset] - array[i] \n5. Track maximum difference value and store its index position\n6. If no positive differences found, calculate proportional fallback value\n7. Store index of maximum difference in pnMaxDiffIndex output parameter\n8. Return maximum difference value or calculated proportional result\n\nParameters:\ndwEndIndex - Upper bound index for array processing range (exclusive)\npanArray - Pointer to integer array containing frame size or buffer data values\ndwStartIndex - Lower bound index for array processing range (inclusive)  \npnMaxDiffIndex - Output pointer to store index where maximum difference occurred\n\nReturns:\nMaximum difference value found between consecutive elements in specified range\nIf no differences found, returns proportional calculation: ((array[dwEndIndex] - array[0]) * dwStartIndex) / dwEndIndex\nZero if input range is invalid (dwEndIndex <= dwStartIndex)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nRange validation prevents processing when dwEndIndex <= dwStartIndex\nProportional fallback used when all consecutive differences are zero or negative\nDivision by zero prevented by range validation ensuring dwEndIndex > 0",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
