      "name": "FloatToLong",
      "signature": "longlong FloatToLong(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "longlong",
      "comment": "Visual Studio C Runtime Library floating-point to long conversion function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up stack frame and allocate 12 bytes for local storage\n2. Store current FPU control word to preserve rounding mode\n3. Load current FPU control word into AX register\n4. Set FPU rounding mode to truncate (OR AH with 0x0C)\n5. Store modified control word and load it into FPU\n6. Convert ST(0) floating-point value to 64-bit integer using FISTP\n7. Restore original FPU control word to maintain caller state\n8. Load 64-bit result into EAX:EDX register pair for return\n9. Clean up stack frame and return to caller\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT in_ST0 (float10): Extended precision floating-point value on FPU stack top\n\nReturns:\nlonglong: 64-bit signed integer result of truncating conversion\n- Returns truncated integer value (toward zero)\n- Handles full range of 64-bit signed integers\n- Preserves FPU state for caller\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFPU Control Word manipulation ensures truncation toward zero rather than banker's rounding\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0C (hex) = 12 (decimal): FPU control word RC field bits for truncate mode\n- Sets both RC1 and RC0 bits to force truncation rounding\n- Temporarily overrides default rounding mode during conversion\n\nNote: Function uses 3 stack-allocated temporary variables optimized away by decompiler:\n- Two 16-bit FPU control words for save/restore operations  \n- One 64-bit storage location for FISTP instruction output",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
