      "name": "InitializeHuffmanDecoder",
      "signature": "void InitializeHuffmanDecoder(BitstreamContext * pContext, BitstreamContext * pBitstream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize Huffman decoder with bitstream context and lookup tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract pointers to specific fields within the context structure\n2. Pass table size pointer (context + 0x24) to decoder function\n3. Pass table index pointer (context + 0x20) to decoder function  \n4. Pass decoded data buffer pointer (context + 0x10) to decoder function\n5. Call FUN_10003cb0 to perform actual Huffman table initialization\n\nParameters:\n- pContext (BitstreamContext *): Decoder context structure containing bitstream state\n- pBitstream (BitstreamContext *): Secondary bitstream context for table data\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function modifies context structure in-place\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name        | Type    | Description\n-------|------|-------------------|---------|------------------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | pBitBuffer        | uint *  | Pointer to current position in bit buffer\n0x04   | 4    | nBytesRemaining   | int     | Number of bytes remaining to process\n0x08   | 4    | dwCurrentBits     | uint    | Current bit accumulator\n0x0C   | 4    | nBitsRemaining    | uint    | Number of bits remaining in accumulator\n0x10   | 16   | abDecodedData     | byte[16]| Buffer for decoded Huffman data\n0x20   | 4    | dwTableIndex      | uint    | Huffman table index selector\n0x24   | 4    | dwTableSize       | uint    | Size of current Huffman table\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function is a thin wrapper around FUN_10003cb0 which performs actual initialization\n- Offsets 0x10, 0x20, 0x24 are critical structure fields accessed during decoding\n- Used in video/image decompression context as part of _ExpandPlane@44 function",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
