      "name": "ProcessFftRadix2",
      "signature": "void ProcessFftRadix2(int nSize, float * pfComplexData, int nStride)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Process FFT using radix-2 and radix-4 decimation-in-time algorithm.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if input size > 15, call preprocessing for large transforms\n2. If size > 127, recursively process larger blocks using radix-8 scaling\n3. Determine optimal radix based on remaining size:\n   - For nCurrentSize * 2 < nSize: Apply radix-4 transform\n   - For nCurrentSize * 2 == nSize: Apply radix-2 transform\n4. Radix-4 processing: Butterfly operations on 4 complex number groups\n   - Load complex pairs from 4 quadrants of data array\n   - Apply FFT butterfly: combine real/imaginary components\n   - Store results back to original positions\n5. Radix-2 processing: Simple 2-point FFT butterfly operations\n   - Load complex pairs from 2 positions\n   - Apply basic butterfly: (a+b, a-b) transform\n   - Store results back to array\n\nParameters:\nnSize - Transform size (number of complex samples to process)\npfComplexData - Interleaved complex data array [real0,imag0,real1,imag1,...]\nnStride - Data stride or processing flags\n\nReturns:\nvoid (in-place transform of pfComplexData array)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf nSize <= 15: Skip preprocessing, use small transform optimization\nIf nCurrentSize <= 0: Skip butterfly processing entirely\nRecursive calls handle nSize > 127 with block size scaling by factor 8\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0F (15) - Threshold for small transform optimization\n0x7F (127) - Threshold for recursive large transform processing  \n0x10 (16) - Initial block size for large transforms\n0x80 (128) - Starting block size for recursive calls\n0x08 (8) - Scaling factor for recursive block size progression\n\nStructure Layout:\nComplex numbers stored as interleaved real/imaginary pairs:\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type   Description\n+0      4     real          float  Real component\n+4      4     imaginary     float  Imaginary component\n\nFFT Butterfly Operations:\nRadix-2: Two-point transform (a + b, a - b)\nRadix-4: Four-point transform with twiddle factor combinations",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:75c635154499e74b2fac028cc68f00c7",
