      "name": "DllMain",
      "signature": "int DllMain(uint hInstance, int dwReason)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "DLL main entry point handling process attach and detach operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check dwReason parameter to determine attach (1) or detach (0) operation\n2. For ATTACH (dwReason == 1):\n   a. Store Windows version from GetVersion() in global storage\n   b. Call initialization function and verify success\n   c. Extract major/minor version bytes and build composite version\n   d. Store command line pointer from GetCommandLineA()\n   e. Initialize subsystems via sequence of function calls\n   f. Increment global reference counter\n3. For DETACH (dwReason == 0):\n   a. Check if reference counter is valid (>= 1)\n   b. Decrement global reference counter\n   c. Conditionally call cleanup if flag is clear\n   d. Execute shutdown sequence via function calls\n4. Return 1 for success, 0 for failure\n\nParameters:\nhInstance - Module instance handle passed by Windows loader\ndwReason - DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH (1) or DLL_PROCESS_DETACH (0)\n\nReturns:\n1 (TRUE) - DLL loaded/unloaded successfully\n0 (FALSE) - Initialization failed or invalid detach attempt\n\nSpecial Cases:\nATTACH failure: Returns 0 if initialization function fails, preventing DLL load\nDETACH with zero counter: Returns 0 to indicate improper detach sequence\nReference counting: Uses global counter to track attach/detach balance\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1 - DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH constant\n0x0 - DLL_PROCESS_DETACH constant  \n0xff - Byte mask for version extraction\n0x10 - Shift count for high word extraction\n0x100 - Multiplier for version composition (256 decimal)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
