      "name": "HuffmanDecodeBytes",
      "signature": "void HuffmanDecodeBytes(HuffmanDecodeContext * pContext, BitStreamReader * pBitStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Decodes Huffman-compressed bit stream data into output buffer using context-driven symbol tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if output buffer is full (pWritePtr == pWriteEnd)\n2. Load bit stream state from pBitStream (data pointer, bit buffer, bit count)\n3. Read current bit width (dwCurrentBits) from decode context \n4. Extract length field using bit masking with current width\n5. Skip decode if length is zero (empty run-length sequence)\n6. Setup output buffer pointers and advance write position\n7. Read one bit flag to determine decode mode (0=Huffman, 1=RLE)\n8. HUFFMAN MODE: Use two-level table lookup for symbol decode\n   a. Primary lookup using dwTableBits width at pTableBase\n   b. Extract 4-bit length + 4-bit symbol index from lookup result\n   c. Secondary lookup in symbol table at offset 0x10 in context\n   d. Read additional sign bit if symbol non-zero, negate if bit set\n   e. Store decoded byte and continue until all bytes processed\n9. RLE MODE: Extract 4-bit fill value and replicate\n   a. Read 4-bit value from bit stream \n   b. Apply sign bit if value non-zero\n   c. Fill output buffer using optimized 32-bit writes then byte remainder\n10. Update bit stream state and return\n\nParameters:\npContext: HuffmanDecodeContext pointer containing decode tables and output buffer state\n  - pWritePtr/pWriteEnd: Current write position and buffer bounds\n  - dwTableBits: Primary lookup table bit width (typically 8-12 bits)\n  - pTableBase: Primary Huffman lookup table base address\n  - dwCurrentBits: Current symbol bit width for length extraction\n  - pBufferBase: Output buffer base for pointer calculations\n  - abSymbolTable[]: Secondary symbol decode table at offset 0x10\npBitStream: BitStreamReader pointer for bit-packed input data\n  - pData: Current data read position (32-bit aligned)\n  - dwBitBuffer: Accumulated bits for extraction (up to 32 bits)  \n  - dwBitCount: Valid bits remaining in dwBitBuffer (0-31)\n\nReturns:\nVoid function with side effects on context and bit stream state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero length triggers empty buffer setup (pWritePtr = pWriteEnd = pBufferBase + 4)\n- Bit buffer exhaustion triggers automatic 32-bit word reload from stream\n- Symbol table uses 4-bit indices with separate length encoding\n- RLE mode optimizes fills using 32-bit stores for quad-aligned blocks\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1F (31): Maximum bit count mask for shift operations\n0x20 (32): Bits per word, used for bit arithmetic overflow handling\n0x10 (16): Offset to symbol decode table within HuffmanDecodeContext\n0x2C (44): Offset to pBufferBase field (param_1[11])\n0x0F (15): 4-bit mask for symbol index and fill value extraction\n\nStructure Layout:\nHuffmanDecodeContext (estimated 400+ bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type          Description\n------  ----  ----------------  -----------   ---------------------------\n0x00    4     pWritePtr         byte *        Current write position\n0x04    4     pWriteEnd         byte *        End of write buffer\n0x20    4     dwTableBits       uint          Primary lookup bit width  \n0x24    4     pTableBase        byte *        Primary lookup table\n0x28    4     dwCurrentBits     uint          Current symbol bit width\n0x2C    4     pBufferBase       byte *        Output buffer base\n0x10+   256   abSymbolTable     byte[256]     Secondary symbol table\n\nBitStreamReader (16 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type          Description  \n------  ----  ----------------  -----------   ---------------------------\n0x00    4     pData             uint *        Current read position\n0x04    4     pSaved            uint *        Saved pointer state  \n0x08    4     dwBitBuffer       uint          Accumulated input bits\n0x0C    4     dwBitCount        uint          Valid bits in buffer\n\nFlag Bits:\nBit 0: Decode mode flag (0=Huffman table decode, 1=RLE fill mode)\nLookup Result Format: [7:4]=length bits, [3:0]=symbol table index\n\nError Handling:\n- No explicit error checking, assumes valid input stream and sufficient buffer space\n- Automatic bit reload prevents buffer underflow during normal operation\n- Context validation through pWritePtr boundary comparison",
