      "name": "OptimizeRectangleSplit",
      "signature": "int OptimizeRectangleSplit(int * pOutputRect1, int * pOutputRect2, int * pSourceRect, int nParam4, int nParam5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Analyzes a source rectangle and attempts to find the optimal way to split it into two sub-rectangles to maximize area utilization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if source rectangle width is >= 32 pixels for horizontal split eligibility\n2. If horizontal split possible:\n   - Copy source rectangle coordinates to temporary rectangle structure\n   - Calculate horizontal split point as (width / 2) aligned to 16-pixel boundary  \n   - Create first sub-rectangle: original X, original width = split point\n   - Create second sub-rectangle: X + split point, width = remaining width\n   - Process both sub-rectangles through helper function\n   - Calculate horizontal area gain: original area - (first area + second area)\n3. Check if source rectangle height is >= 32 pixels for vertical split eligibility\n4. If vertical split possible:\n   - Copy source rectangle coordinates to temporary rectangle structure\n   - Calculate vertical split point as (height / 2) aligned to 16-pixel boundary\n   - Create first sub-rectangle: original Y, original height = split point\n   - Create second sub-rectangle: Y + split point, height = remaining height  \n   - Process both sub-rectangles through helper function\n   - Calculate vertical area gain: original area - (first area + second area)\n5. Compare horizontal vs vertical area gains and select optimal split\n6. If vertical split is better, copy vertical split results to output rectangles\n7. Return the better area gain value\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputRect1: Pointer to RECT structure receiving first split rectangle (left/top portion)\n- pOutputRect2: Pointer to RECT structure receiving second split rectangle (right/bottom portion)  \n- pSourceRect: Pointer to source RECT structure to be split (left, top, right, bottom)\n- nParam4: Processing parameter passed to helper function (usage unknown)\n- nParam5: Processing parameter passed to helper function (usage unknown)\n\nReturns:\n- Area gain value (int): Amount of area recovered by optimal splitting\n- 0: If no split was possible (rectangle too small in both dimensions)\n- Positive value: Area gain from successful split operation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Rectangles smaller than 32 pixels in width cannot be split horizontally\n- Rectangles smaller than 32 pixels in height cannot be split vertically  \n- Both dimensions must be >= 32 for any splitting to occur\n- Split points are aligned to 16-pixel boundaries (split_point = ((dimension / 2) + 15) & 0xFFFFFFF0)\n- If neither split is possible, function returns 0 and output rectangles remain unchanged\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x20 (32): Minimum dimension size required for splitting in either direction\n- 0xF (15): Alignment mask addend for 16-pixel boundary alignment\n- 0xFFFFFFF0: Mask for 16-pixel boundary alignment (clears low 4 bits)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
