      "name": "ProcessYuvToRgbConversion",
      "signature": "void ProcessYuvToRgbConversion(int nPixelPairCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts YUV color data to RGB format using optimized lookup tables for video processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize chroma buffer pointers and extract initial U/V chroma components\n2. Calculate base color lookup values from Y (luminance), U and V (chroma) components\n3. Enter main processing loop for pixel pairs:\n   a. Read luminance value from destination buffer and convert to lookup index\n   b. Extract RGB color components using precomputed lookup tables\n   c. Pack color components using CONCAT operations for efficient 32-bit writes\n   d. Write converted RGB data to source buffer with proper stride (6-byte advance)\n   e. Update chroma buffer pointers and recalculate lookup values\n   f. Process second pixel of the pair with similar operations\n   g. Advance to next buffer position and decrement pixel pair counter\n4. Process end buffer using identical conversion logic with separate buffer pointers\n5. Restore chroma buffer pointers to previous positions (backtrack by 1)\n\nParameters:\nnPixelPairCount - Number of pixel pairs to convert (int)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Conversion performed in-place using global buffer pointers\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction processes pixels in pairs for efficiency, using shared chroma data\nGlobal buffer pointers are automatically advanced during processing\nChroma pointers are restored at end to enable subsequent processing passes\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x4 - Lookup table stride for 32-bit color values\n0x6 - Source buffer advance (6 bytes per processed pixel pair)\n0x18 - Left shift by 24 bits for alpha channel positioning\n0x10 - Right shift by 16 bits for color component extraction\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error checking - assumes valid global buffer pointers and lookup tables\nFunction relies on caller to ensure sufficient buffer space and valid pixel count\n\nGlobal Buffer Dependencies:\ng_pChromaBufferU - Pointer to U component chroma data buffer\ng_pChromaBufferV - Pointer to V component chroma data buffer  \ng_pDstBufferCurrent - Pointer to current position in destination luminance buffer\ng_pDstBufferEnd - Pointer to end position in destination luminance buffer\ng_pSrcBufferCurrent - Pointer to current position in source RGB output buffer\ng_pSrcBufferEnd - Pointer to end position in source RGB output buffer\n\nLookup Table Dependencies:\ng_adYToRedLookupTable - Luminance to red component conversion table\ng_adVToRedLookupTable - V chroma to red component conversion table\ng_adYToGreenLookupTable - Luminance to green component conversion table\ng_adUToBlueLookupTable - U chroma to blue component conversion table\ng_adLuminanceBaseLookupTable - Base luminance value lookup table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
