      "comment": "Merges two input byte streams into a single output stream based on bit flags from a bit stream state machine.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Initialize second source counter from first source counter\n2. Main processing loop until both counters reach zero:\n   a. Check if bit stream counter is empty (== 0)\n   b. If empty: Read next 32-bit value from bit stream, set counter to 31 (0x1F)\n   c. If not empty: Use current bit value and decrement counter\n   d. Extract least significant bit from current bit value\n   e. Right-shift bit value by 1 for next iteration\n   f. If bit is 0: Copy byte from source1 to output, increment pointers, decrement source1 counter\n   g. If bit is 1: Copy byte from source2 to output, increment pointers, decrement source2 counter\n   h. Always increment output pointer after copying\n   i. Continue until one source is exhausted\n3. Drain remaining bytes from non-empty source to output\n4. Return when both sources are exhausted\n\nParameters:\n\npBitStream    - Pointer to bit stream state structure containing bit data pointer, current bits, and bit counter\npbOutput      - Output buffer where merged bytes are written\npbSource1     - First input stream (selected when bit = 0)\npbSource2     - Second input stream (selected when bit = 1)\nnSource1Count - Number of bytes available in first source stream\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value, operates by side effects on output buffer and input stream pointers\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- If source1 is exhausted first, remaining source2 bytes are copied directly\n- If source2 is exhausted first, remaining source1 bytes are copied directly\n- Function handles cases where both sources are exhausted simultaneously\n- Bit stream automatically refills from next 32-bit word when counter reaches zero\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x1F (31) - Maximum bit counter value after reading new 32-bit word\n0x01      - Bit mask for extracting least significant bit\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nBitStream structure (16 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name     Type      Description\n0x00    4     pBitData       uint *    Pointer to current 32-bit word in bit stream\n0x04    4     (unknown)      uint      Reserved or padding field\n0x08    4     dwCurrentBits  uint      Current 32-bit value being processed\n0x0C    4     nBitCounter    uint      Number of remaining bits in current word (0-31)",
