      "name": "PerformIdct2d8x8",
      "signature": "void PerformIdct2d8x8(char * pbOutputBuffer, int nStride, short * pDctCoefficients, int nCosineTableOffset, char * pbReferenceBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Performs 2D 8x8 Inverse Discrete Cosine Transform (IDCT) on DCT coefficients.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize cosine coefficient table pointer using base address + offset * 256\n2. Set up DCT coefficient pointer and working buffer pointer\n3. Perform 1D IDCT on each column (8 iterations):\n   a. Check if all AC coefficients in column are zero (optimization path)\n   b. If all zero: multiply DC coefficient by cosine table and replicate across column\n   c. If non-zero: perform full 1D IDCT using butterfly operations with fixed-point arithmetic\n   d. Apply scaling factors 0xb50, 0xec8, -0x14e8, 0x8a9 for frequency domain transforms\n   e. Store intermediate results in transform buffer with 8x8 stride\n4. Perform 1D IDCT on each row (8 iterations):\n   a. Load 8 values from transform buffer with column spacing\n   b. Apply same butterfly transform as column processing\n   c. Add rounding offset 0x7f and right-shift by 8 for final scaling\n   d. Add reference buffer values for motion compensation\n   e. Clamp to byte range and store in output buffer\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputBuffer: Output image buffer to store final pixel values\n- nStride: Row stride in bytes for output buffer navigation\n- pDctCoefficients: 8x8 matrix of DCT coefficients (16-bit signed values)\n- nCosineTableOffset: Offset index into global cosine coefficient table\n- pReferenceBuffer: Reference frame buffer for motion compensation\n\nReturns:\n- void (performs in-place transformation to output buffer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Optimized path for columns with zero AC coefficients (DC-only)\n- Fixed-point arithmetic with 11-bit fractional precision (>> 0xb scaling)\n- Final output includes 0x7f rounding bias before 8-bit conversion\n- Motion compensation adds reference pixel values to transformed coefficients\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0xb: Right shift count for 11-bit fixed-point scaling\n- 0xb50: Fixed-point coefficient for cos(\u03c0/8) \u00d7 2048 = 2896\n- 0xec8: Fixed-point coefficient for cos(3\u03c0/8) \u00d7 2048 = 3784\n- -0x14e8: Fixed-point coefficient for -cos(3\u03c0/8) \u00d7 sin(\u03c0/4) \u00d7 2048 = -5352\n- 0x8a9: Fixed-point coefficient for cos(\u03c0/8) \u00d7 sin(\u03c0/4) \u00d7 2048 = 2217\n- 0x7f: Rounding bias (127) added before final 8-bit conversion\n- 0x100: 256-byte spacing between cosine table entries\n- 8: 8x8 block size for both row and column processing\n\nStructure Layout:\nTransform Buffer (anTransformBuffer[64]):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name           Type    Description\n  0x00    4     anTransformBuffer[0] int     First transformed value\n  0x04    4     anTransformBuffer[1] int     Second transformed value  \n  ...     ...   ...                  ...     8x8 = 64 total coefficients\n  0xFC    4     anTransformBuffer[63] int    Last transformed value\n\nWorkspace Arrays (6 \u00d7 32 bytes each):\n  Each anWorkspace[N] provides temporary storage for intermediate calculations\n  during the two-pass (column then row) IDCT processing.",
