      "name": "InitializeColorConversionState",
      "signature": "void InitializeColorConversionState(uint dwConversionFlags, int * pnRowBytes, int nWidth, int nHeight, int * pConversionParams, int * pnOutputRowBytes)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Configures color conversion state and lookup tables for YUV to RGB conversion\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reset global conversion error flag to 0\n2. Store input row bytes value to global state\n3. Check initialization mode flag (0x10000) to determine lookup table setup\n   - If flag set and not already initialized: Initialize 8 conversion lookup tables (256 entries each)\n   - If flag clear and tables initialized: Reset tables with 0x800 entries from base table\n4. Check conversion disable flag (0x40000) and global disable state\n5. Extract color space mode from upper bits (0x70000000 mask):\n   - 0x10000000: YUV420 planar mode - allocate buffer, double row bytes, calculate output offset\n   - 0x30000000/0x50000000: YUV422/YUV444 modes - calculate output with -2 stride\n   - 0x40000000: YUV420 packed mode - allocate double buffer, double row bytes\n   - Default: Standard YUV mode - calculate simple output offset\n6. Configure conversion parameters based on progressive/interlaced flag (0x20000)\n   - Sets global pointer offsets for conversion parameter tables\n   - Calls helper functions for quantization setup\n   - Loads clipping and scaling factors from parameter structure\n7. Compare bit precision values to determine output shift amount\n8. Calculate bit mask from shift amount using power-of-2 shift\n\nParameters:\ndwConversionFlags: Conversion mode flags controlling initialization and color space\n  - 0x10000: Initialize lookup tables\n  - 0x20000: Progressive scan mode (vs interlaced)\n  - 0x40000: Force conversion disable\n  - 0x70000000: Color space mode (YUV420/YUV422/YUV444/packed)\npnRowBytes: Pointer to input row bytes value (modified for doubling in some modes)\nnWidth: Image width in pixels\nnHeight: Image height in pixels\npConversionParams: Pointer to conversion parameter structure containing:\n  - Quantization matrices at various offsets\n  - Clipping values and scaling factors\n  - Bit precision settings for output calculation\npnOutputRowBytes: Pointer to output row bytes calculation result\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Results stored in global variables and output parameters\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10000 - Initialize lookup tables flag\n0x20000 - Progressive scan mode flag\n0x40000 - Disable conversion flag\n0x70000000 - Color space mode mask\n0x10000000 - YUV420 planar mode\n0x30000000 - YUV422 mode\n0x40000000 - YUV420 packed mode\n0x50000000 - YUV444 mode\n0x100 - Standard lookup table size (256 entries)\n0x800 - Extended lookup table size (2048 entries)\n\nError Handling:\nGlobal error flag reset at function start\nConversion can be disabled via flag or global state\nParameter structure offsets vary by scan mode",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
