      "name": "BinkNextFrame",
      "signature": "void BinkNextFrame(BinkFileHandle * pBinkHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Advances a Bink video file to the next frame for playback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input handle is not null\n2. Set busy flag at offset 0x134 to prevent concurrent access  \n3. Get current system time using timeGetTime()\n4. Call FUN_10009770 to update internal timing state\n5. Compare current frame index (offset 0xc) with total frames (offset 0x8)\n6. If current < total: increment frame index by 1\n7. If current >= total: reset frame index to 1 (loop back to start)\n8. Call BinkPositionFrame to seek to calculated frame position\n9. Clear busy flag at offset 0x134 to allow further operations\n\nParameters:\npBinkHandle - Pointer to BinkFileHandle structure containing video state\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; function operates on handle state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null handle: Function exits immediately without processing\n- Frame wraparound: When at last frame, loops back to frame 1 (not 0)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type   | Description\n0x08   | 4    | pfnSeek      | uint   | Total frame count  \n0x0C   | 4    | pfnTell      | uint   | Current frame index\n0x134  | 4    | busyFlag     | uint   | Processing busy flag\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x134 (308) - Offset to busy flag in BinkFileHandle structure\n0x08 (8) - Offset to total frame count \n0x0C (12) - Offset to current frame index\n1 - Reset frame index value (first playable frame)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:9911d36575de29f20d789acc2c19c5d5",
