      "name": "ConvertSamples16to8",
      "signature": "void ConvertSamples16to8(byte * pbOutputBuffer, ushort * pwInputSamples, uint dwSampleCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts 16-bit audio samples to 8-bit signed format with offset adjustment\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Calculate loop count as half the sample count (dwSampleCount >> 1)\n2. Iterate through input samples:\n   a. Read 16-bit sample from input buffer (pwInputSamples)\n   b. Extract high byte using right shift by 8 bits\n   c. Apply -0x80 offset adjustment to convert to signed range\n   d. Store result as 8-bit value in output buffer (pbOutputBuffer)\n   e. Advance both input and output pointers\n3. Continue until all samples processed\n\nParameters:\npbOutputBuffer (byte *) - Output buffer for 8-bit converted samples\npwInputSamples (ushort *) - Input buffer containing 16-bit samples\ndwSampleCount (uint) - Total number of bytes to process (actual samples = dwSampleCount/2)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Processes dwSampleCount/2 actual samples since each 16-bit sample is 2 bytes\n- Offset adjustment of -0x80 (decimal -128) converts from unsigned to signed range\n- High byte extraction ((sample >> 8) & 0xFF) effectively divides by 256\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1 - Right shift by 1 bit to calculate sample count from byte count\n0x8 - Right shift by 8 bits to extract high byte of 16-bit sample  \n0x80 - Offset value (decimal 128) subtracted to convert unsigned to signed",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:9a541bcc903ff4ee859ac8534df3ddeb",
