      "name": "BinkBufferSetDirectDraw",
      "signature": "BOOL BinkBufferSetDirectDraw(LPVOID lpDirectDraw, LPVOID lpDirectDrawSurface)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "BOOL",
      "comment": "Configures DirectDraw objects for Bink video buffer operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters are non-null (both DirectDraw object and surface)\n2. If either parameter is null, clear all global DirectDraw state and return success\n3. If both parameters are valid, store DirectDraw object and surface in globals\n4. Set DirectDraw flags to 0x8000000 (134217728) to enable acceleration mode\n5. Call internal initialization function FUN_10005600 to complete setup\n6. Return TRUE to indicate successful configuration\n\nParameters:\nlpDirectDraw - Pointer to DirectDraw object interface (IDirectDraw*)\nlpDirectDrawSurface - Pointer to DirectDraw surface interface (IDirectDrawSurface*)\n\nReturns:\nTRUE - Always returns success (both for valid setup and cleanup operations)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf null parameters provided: Performs cleanup by zeroing all global state\nMagic number 0x8000000 enables hardware acceleration mode for video operations\n\nState Variables:\ng_lpDirectDraw - Stores DirectDraw object pointer globally\ng_lpDirectDrawSurface - Stores DirectDraw surface pointer globally  \ng_dwDirectDrawFlags - DirectDraw configuration flags (0x8000000 = acceleration enabled)\n\nError Handling:\nFunction always returns TRUE regardless of input validity\nNo error conditions reported - cleanup mode for invalid inputs",
