      "name": "InitializeDirectDrawD3D",
      "signature": "void InitializeDirectDrawD3D(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize DirectDraw and create D3D device for video rendering\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if DirectDraw is already initialized (g_dwDirectDrawFlags != 0)\n2. If already initialized, increment reference counter and return\n3. Check DirectDraw version availability (g_dwDirectDrawVersion)\n4. If version < 0x20 (minimum required), return early\n5. Call DirectDraw creation function via g_pfnDirectDrawCreate\n6. Validate display mode settings (width, height, color depth)\n7. Create DirectDraw interface and set cooperative level\n8. If display mode parameters valid, set display mode\n9. Clear D3D device buffer and initialize parameters\n10. Create D3D device interface with 108-byte structure\n11. Call DetectD3DCapabilities to probe hardware features\n12. Increment DirectDraw reference counter on success\n13. Release DirectDraw interface on failure\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if DirectDraw already initialized\n- Early return if DirectDraw version insufficient (< 0x20)\n- Clear display flags if any dimension parameter is zero\n- Release DirectDraw interface if D3D device creation fails\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x20 - Minimum DirectDraw version required\n0x50 - DirectDraw interface SetCooperativeLevel method offset\n0x54 - DirectDraw interface SetDisplayMode method offset  \n0x18 - DirectDraw interface CreateDevice method offset\n0x08 - DirectDraw interface Release method offset\n0x6c - Size of D3D device creation structure (108 bytes)\n0x1b - Loop counter for clearing 27 DWORDs (108 bytes / 4)\n0x200 - D3D device flags value",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:9dbe11483c0e42ddf5d87ee4d23fa5ba",
