      "name": "ProcessYuvToRgbYuy2Blit",
      "signature": "void ProcessYuvToRgbYuy2Blit(uint dwSrcX, uint dwSrcY, int nSrcPitch, uint dwSrcWidth, uint dwSrcHeight, uint dwDstX, uint dwDstY, uint dwDstHeight, uint dwDstWidth, uint dwDstPitch, byte * pSrcBuffer, byte * pDstBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Process YUV YUY2 format video buffer to RGB color conversion with boundary alignment\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check source X coordinate alignment - if LSB 2 bits equal 2, increment Y and align X to 4-byte boundary\n2. Handle source Y coordinate odd/even alignment based on destination requirements\n3. If source Y is odd, adjust destination Y and height accordingly to maintain field alignment\n4. If source Y is even, check destination Y alignment and adjust if needed\n5. Ensure destination height is even by decrementing if odd (field-based processing)\n6. Call ProcessYuvColorConversion with adjusted parameters and global conversion table\n\nParameters:\n  dwSrcX - Source X coordinate in pixels (aligned to 4-byte boundary if needed)\n  dwSrcY - Source Y coordinate in pixels (field alignment checked)\n  nSrcPitch - Source buffer pitch in bytes (can be negative for bottom-up)\n  dwSrcWidth - Source rectangle width in pixels\n  dwSrcHeight - Source rectangle height in pixels\n  dwDstX - Destination X coordinate in pixels\n  dwDstY - Destination Y coordinate in pixels (adjusted for field alignment)\n  dwDstHeight - Destination rectangle height in pixels (forced to even)\n  dwDstWidth - Destination rectangle width in pixels\n  dwDstPitch - Destination buffer pitch in bytes\n  pSrcBuffer - Pointer to source YUV YUY2 video data buffer\n  pDstBuffer - Pointer to destination RGB video data buffer\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function does not return a value, conversion performed in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Alignment Handling: Source X alignment to 0x02 triggers Y increment and X masking to 0xFFFFFFFC\n  Field Processing: Odd Y coordinates require height adjustment to maintain proper field alignment\n  Height Normalization: Destination height forced to even values for field-based video processing\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x02 - X coordinate alignment check value for 4-byte boundary detection  \n  0x03 - Bit mask for checking 2 LSBs of coordinates\n  0xFFFFFFFC - Bit mask for aligning X coordinate to 4-byte boundary\n  0x01 - Odd/even check mask for Y coordinates and height values\n\nStructure Layout:\nYuvConversionEntry (16 bytes total):\n| Offset | Size | Field Name     | Type | Description                    |\n|--------|------|----------------|------|--------------------------------|\n| 0x00   | 4    | dwCoeffA       | uint | First conversion coefficient   |\n| 0x04   | 4    | dwCoeffB       | uint | Second conversion coefficient  |\n| 0x08   | 4    | pLookupTable   | uint | Pointer to lookup table        |\n| 0x0C   | 4    | dwTableSize    | uint | Size of lookup table entries   |\n\nError Handling:\n  No explicit error handling - assumes valid buffer pointers and dimensions\n  Conversion parameters validated in called ProcessYuvColorConversion function",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
