      "name": "ClearBitArrayRange",
      "signature": "void ClearBitArrayRange(uint * pBitArray, int nBitIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Clears a specific bit and all corresponding bits in preceding elements of a bit array\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate target element index: nElementIndex = nBitIndex / 0x20 (32 bits per uint)\n2. Calculate bit position within element: nBitPosition = nBitIndex % 0x20\n3. Create bit mask for target bit: 1 << (0x1f - nBitPosition)\n4. Call FUN_10021de7 to clear the specific bit in target element\n5. Decrement element index and iterate backward through array\n6. For each preceding element, call FUN_10021de7 to clear bit 0 (0x01 mask)\n7. Continue until reaching beginning of array (nElementIndex < 0)\n\nParameters:\npBitArray - Base pointer to uint array representing bit array\nnBitIndex - Zero-based bit index to clear (also determines range)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf nBitIndex < 32, only processes element 0\nIf FUN_10021de7 returns 0 during backward iteration, function returns early\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x20 (32) - Bits per array element (uint size)\n0x1f (31) - Bit position mask (32-1)\n0x04 (4)  - Bytes per array element (uint size)\n0x01 (1)  - Lowest bit mask for clearing bit 0 in preceding elements\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit validation of pBitArray or nBitIndex\nFunction assumes valid inputs and properly allocated array",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a1fd1f83ab5d96b4bef4e8817dd3ae88",
