      "name": "FormatFloatToString",
      "signature": "void FormatFloatToString(double * pdValue, char * lpszBuffer, size_t nBufferSize, int nPrecision)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts a floating-point number to string representation with precision control.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load double precision value from input pointer onto FPU stack\n2. Call FUN_100202f7() to obtain floating-point formatting context structure\n3. Store context pointer and extract precision from context[1] - 1\n4. Check for negative sign in first element of context (0x2d = ASCII '-')\n5. Call FUN_10020280() to perform initial formatting with adjusted buffer pointer\n6. Update precision tracking flags and recalculate precision limit\n7. Validate precision bounds (-4 minimum) and buffer size constraints\n8. If precision out of range OR buffer too small: call FUN_1001e1d9() for full formatting\n9. Otherwise for normal case: adjust buffer pointer past sign if needed\n10. If precision tracking flag set: find string end and truncate last character\n11. Call FUN_1001e200() for final formatting with truncated buffer\n\nParameters:\n- pdValue: Pointer to double precision floating-point value to convert\n- lpszBuffer: Output string buffer to receive formatted result\n- nBufferSize: Size of output buffer in bytes\n- nPrecision: Formatting precision specifier passed to sub-formatters\n\nReturns:\n- void (result written to lpszBuffer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Negative values: Sign character (0x2d) detected and buffer adjusted accordingly\n- Precision limits: Values below -4 trigger full formatting path\n- Buffer overflow: Small buffers relative to precision trigger full formatting\n- String truncation: Last character removed when precision tracking enabled\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x2d (45): ASCII minus sign character for negative detection\n- -4: Minimum precision threshold for simplified formatting path\n- 0x1003c8ec: Global pointer to floating-point formatting context structure\n- 0x1003c8f4: Global precision tracking value\n- 0x1003c8f8: Global flag indicating precision adjustment needed\n\nError Handling:\n- Buffer size validation prevents overflow in normal formatting path\n- Precision bounds checking routes edge cases to robust full formatter\n- Out-of-range conditions handled by FUN_1001e1d9() fallback\n\nStructure Layout:\nFloating-point context structure (from FUN_100202f7):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x0    | 4    | nSignFlag  | int  | Sign indicator (0x2d for negative)\n0x4    | 4    | nPrecision | int  | Base precision value for calculations",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
