      "name": "RaiseFpuException",
      "signature": "void RaiseFpuException(FpuExceptionContext * pContext, uint * pStatusWord, uint dwExceptionFlags, uint dwExceptionParam, double * pOperand1, double * pOperand2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts FPU exception flags to Windows structured exception and raises it through kernel32.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize exception context structure fields to zero (dwExceptionInformationFlags, dwFpuFlags, dwReserved)\n2. Translate FPU exception flags to Windows exception codes:\n   - 0x10 (Stack underflow) -> 0xC000008F (STATUS_FLOAT_UNDERFLOW) + flag bit 0x1\n   - 0x02 (Denormalized operand) -> 0xC0000093 (STATUS_FLOAT_INEXACT_RESULT) + flag bit 0x2  \n   - 0x01 (Invalid operation) -> 0xC0000091 (STATUS_FLOAT_INVALID_OPERATION) + flag bit 0x4\n   - 0x04 (Division by zero) -> 0xC000008E (STATUS_FLOAT_DIVIDE_BY_ZERO) + flag bit 0x8\n   - 0x08 (Overflow) -> 0xC0000090 (STATUS_FLOAT_OVERFLOW) + flag bit 0x10\n3. Capture inverted status word flags and encode into context dwFpuFlags field\n4. Call FUN_1001e8df() to get additional FPU status and encode into dwReserved field  \n5. Decode rounding mode from status word (bits 10-11) and encode into context control flags\n6. Decode precision control from status word (bits 8-9) and encode into context control flags\n7. Embed exception parameter (bits 0-11) into context control flags (bits 5-16)\n8. Store operand values and set operand control flags for exception context\n9. Call FUN_1001e8ed() for cleanup before exception\n10. Raise Windows structured exception via RaiseException() with prepared context\n11. After exception handling, restore original status word flags from context\n12. Decode and restore rounding mode to status word\n13. Decode and restore precision control to status word  \n14. Return operand2 value to caller\n\nParameters:\npContext - FpuExceptionContext pointer to exception information structure\npStatusWord - uint pointer to FPU status word for flag manipulation\ndwExceptionFlags - uint containing FPU exception flags (bits 0-4: Invalid=0x1, Denorm=0x2, DivZero=0x4, Overflow=0x8, Underflow=0x10)\ndwExceptionParam - uint exception parameter value (embedded in bits 5-16 of context)\npOperand1 - double pointer to first operand value  \npOperand2 - double pointer to second operand value\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Does not return normally, raises structured exception\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction calls RaiseException which transfers control to exception handler\nIf exception handler continues execution, restores FPU state and returns normally\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xC000008F - STATUS_FLOAT_UNDERFLOW (Windows exception code)\n0xC0000093 - STATUS_FLOAT_INEXACT_RESULT (Windows exception code)\n0xC0000091 - STATUS_FLOAT_INVALID_OPERATION (Windows exception code)  \n0xC000008E - STATUS_FLOAT_DIVIDE_BY_ZERO (Windows exception code)\n0xC0000090 - STATUS_FLOAT_OVERFLOW (Windows exception code)\n0xC00 - FPU rounding mode mask (bits 10-11)\n0x300 - FPU precision control mask (bits 8-9)\n0xFFF - Exception parameter mask (bits 0-11)\n\nStructure Layout:\nFpuExceptionContext (88 bytes total):\nOffset | Size | Field Name                  | Type   | Description\n   0   |  4   | dwControlFlags              | uint   | Exception control and rounding mode\n   4   |  4   | dwExceptionInformationFlags | uint   | Translated FPU exception flags  \n   8   |  4   | dwFpuFlags                  | uint   | Inverted status word flags\n  12   |  4   | dwReserved                  | uint   | Additional FPU status from FUN_1001e8df\n  16   |  8   | dblOperand1                 | double | First operand value\n  32   |  4   | dwOperand1Flags             | uint   | Control flags for operand1\n  64   |  8   | dblOperand2                 | double | Second operand value  \n  80   |  4   | dwOperand2Flags             | uint   | Control flags for operand2",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
