      "name": "ProcessPixelDataWithMmxBlending",
      "signature": "void ProcessPixelDataWithMmxBlending(int nPixelCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Process pixel data using MMX SIMD instructions for efficient color channel blending.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load 64-bit blend mask (0x8080808080808080) into MMX register MM1\n2. Initialize source buffer pointer and calculate end address (current + nPixelCount * 4 dwords)\n3. Loop through pixel pairs processing two 32-bit pixels per iteration:\n   a. Load first 32-bit pixel from destination buffer end, increment pointer\n   b. Extract pixel bytes using bit shifts (alpha=>>24, red=>>16, green=>>8, blue=&0xFF)\n   c. Load corresponding mask bytes from the 64-bit blend constant\n   d. Perform MMX PUNPCKLBW operations to interleave pixel and mask bytes\n   e. Store 64-bit result to source buffer end with +8 byte offset\n   f. Load second 32-bit pixel from destination buffer current, increment pointer\n   g. Extract bytes and perform identical MMX blending operations\n   h. Store 64-bit result to source buffer current position\n   i. Advance source buffer current by 16 bytes (4 dwords)\n4. Continue until source buffer current reaches calculated end address\n5. Update global buffer pointers before return\n\nParameters:\nnPixelCount (int): Number of pixel pairs to process (actual pixels = nPixelCount * 2)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nLoop processes pixel pairs, so nPixelCount represents pairs not individual pixels.\nMMX registers are not explicitly cleared - caller responsible for EMMS instruction.\nBlend mask 0x8080808080808080 provides consistent alpha blending coefficients.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8080808080808080 (g_qwMmxBlendMask): 64-bit MMX alpha blend mask\n0x18 (24): Bit shift for alpha channel extraction\n0x10 (16): Bit shift for red channel extraction  \n0x8 (8): Bit shift for green channel extraction\n0x20, 0x28, 0x30, 0x38 (32, 40, 48, 56): Bit shifts for mask byte extraction\n\nGlobal Buffer Usage:\ng_pSrcBufferCurrent: Source pixel buffer write pointer, advanced by nPixelCount*16 bytes\ng_pSrcBufferEnd: Source pixel buffer boundary write pointer, advanced by 16 bytes per iteration\ng_pDstBufferCurrent: Destination pixel buffer read pointer, advanced by 4 bytes per iteration  \ng_pDstBufferEnd: Destination pixel buffer boundary read pointer, advanced by 4 bytes per iteration\n\nMMX Instruction Sequence:\nMOVQ: Load 64-bit blend mask constant\nMOVD: Load 32-bit pixel data into MMX register\nPUNPCKLBW: Unpack low bytes with interleaving for alpha blending\nPUNPCKHBW: Unpack high bytes with interleaving for extended precision",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a67df02b5f56b4265404723e57bd78f3",
