      "name": "ProcessYuvToRgbConversionMMX",
      "signature": "void ProcessYuvToRgbConversionMMX(int nImageWidth)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes YUV to RGB color space conversion using optimized MMX SIMD instructions for enhanced performance.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load MMX conversion coefficients and bias values from global data tables\n2. Initialize source buffer pointers based on image width parameter \n3. Enter first processing loop for current buffer section:\n   a. Load two consecutive 32-bit pixels from destination buffer\n   b. Unpack bytes to words using PUNPCKLBW with zero extension\n   c. Subtract bias using PSUBUSW (unsigned saturated word subtraction)\n   d. Apply YUV multiplication coefficients using PMULHW (packed multiply high words)\n   e. Add offset bias using PADDSW then subtract using PSUBUSW for clamping\n   f. Extract coefficient words from packed conversion table\n   g. Multiply results by final coefficients using PMULLW \n   h. Store converted 64-bit results to source buffer locations\n   i. Advance buffer pointers by 8 bytes (2 pixels) and 16 bytes respectively\n4. Continue loop until source buffer reaches calculated end position\n5. Enter second processing loop for end buffer section using same algorithm\n6. Update global buffer end pointer to final position\n\nParameters:\nnImageWidth (int): Width of image in pixels, used to calculate buffer stride and end positions\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function modifies global buffer contents directly\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Processes image data in two separate phases using different global buffer sets\n- Uses saturated arithmetic to prevent overflow/underflow during color conversion\n- MMX registers maintain packed 16-bit word format throughout processing\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x4A85 (19077): YUV luminance conversion coefficient (\u22481.164 * 16384)\n0x007F (127): Bias offset value for color component normalization\n0x8080 (32896): Packed bias values for unsigned to signed conversion\n\nStructure Layout:\nMMX register format (64-bit packed):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type   | Description\n   0   |  2   | word0      | ushort | First 16-bit color component\n   2   |  2   | word1      | ushort | Second 16-bit color component  \n   4   |  2   | word2      | ushort | Third 16-bit color component\n   6   |  2   | word3      | ushort | Fourth 16-bit color component",
