      "name": "BinkGetTrackType",
      "signature": "int BinkGetTrackType(BINK * pBink, int nTrackIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Retrieves the track type for a specific track in a Bink video file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Validate input handle - check if pBink pointer is not null\n2. If handle is null, return 0 (invalid track type)\n3. Access Bink structure at offset 0x1f0 to get track type array pointer\n4. Calculate track type entry address: base_array + (nTrackIndex * 4)\n5. Return 32-bit track type value from calculated address\n\nParameters:\n\npBink (BINK *): Handle to Bink video file structure, must not be null\nnTrackIndex (int): Zero-based index of track to query type for\n\nReturns:\n\nint: Track type identifier (format-specific constant)\n     0 if pBink handle is null or invalid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nTrack type array located at offset 0x1f0 within Bink structure\nEach track type entry is 4 bytes (32-bit integer)\nFunction performs no bounds checking on nTrackIndex\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x1f0 (496): Offset to track type array pointer in Bink structure\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type  | Description\n-------|------|------------|-------|-------------\n0x000  | 496  | padding1   | byte  | Reserved fields and data\n0x1f0  | 4    | pTrackTypes| int*  | Pointer to track type array",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
