      "name": "BinkAdjustPlaybackTiming",
      "signature": "void BinkAdjustPlaybackTiming(void * pBinkDecoder, int nCurrentTime)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Adjusts Bink video playback timing by accounting for timing gaps\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if decoder has stored pause timestamp (offset 0x208)\n2. If stored timestamp exists, calculate time gap (current time - stored timestamp)\n3. Add calculated time gap to accumulated playback adjustment (offset 0x240)\n4. Clear the stored timestamp to indicate timing has been adjusted\n\nParameters:\npBinkDecoder - Pointer to BinkDecoder structure containing timing state\nnCurrentTime - Current playback time in milliseconds\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x208  | 4    | dwPauseTime| int  | Stored timestamp when pause occurred (0 = not paused)\n0x240  | 4    | dwTimingAdj| int  | Accumulated timing adjustment in milliseconds\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If dwPauseTime is 0, function returns immediately (no timing adjustment needed)\n- Negative time gaps are allowed (backwards time adjustment)\n- Function is called during resume operations to maintain smooth playback",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a8c7f43cc1a5ca6057d221f2392511d8",
