      "name": "SetAudioVolume",
      "signature": "void SetAudioVolume(BinkAudioProcessor * pAudioProcessor, uint dwVolumeInput)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets the volume level for a Bink audio processor with scaling and clamping.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate scaled volume: (dwVolumeInput * 0x7f) / 0x10000 using 64-bit multiplication\n2. Clamp result to maximum value of 0x7f (127) if overflow occurs\n3. Store calculated volume at offset 0x5c in the audio processor structure\n4. Call registered volume change callback with audio handle and new volume level\n\nParameters:\npAudioProcessor - Pointer to BinkAudioProcessor structure containing audio state\ndwVolumeInput - Input volume value to be scaled (range depends on source)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x7f (127) - Maximum volume level in 7-bit range (0-127)\n0x10000 (65536) - Scaling divisor for 16-bit to 7-bit conversion\n0x44 - Offset to audio handle/identifier field in BinkAudioProcessor\n0x5c - Offset to current volume field in BinkAudioProcessor\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Input values above threshold will be clamped to 0x7f to prevent overflow\n- Callback function pointer may be NULL (not validated before call)\n- Volume calculation uses 64-bit intermediate to prevent 32-bit overflow\n\nStructure Layout:\nBinkAudioProcessor structure (relevant fields):\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type     Description\n0x44    4     dwAudioHandle        uint     Audio device/stream identifier\n0x5c    4     dwCurrentVolume      uint     Current volume level (0-127)",
