      "name": "DecodeBitStreamToShorts",
      "signature": "void DecodeBitStreamToShorts(DecoderContext * pDecoderCtx, BitStreamReader * pBitReader)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Decodes variable-length encoded data from bit stream into array of signed shorts.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate decoder context by checking current position equals end position\n2. Extract bit width configuration from decoder context (typically 8-16 bits)\n3. Read initial code value using variable-length bit extraction\n4. If code is 0, perform fast skip operation by updating pointers and exit\n5. Read data value using configured bit width (signed or unsigned mode)\n6. For signed mode, extract sign bit and apply two's complement if negative\n7. Store first decoded value to output buffer and initialize accumulators\n8. Enter main decoding loop for remaining elements:\n   a. Read 4-bit length code for run-length or literal count\n   b. If length is 0, perform run-length expansion of previous value\n   c. Otherwise, decode specified number of delta values\n   d. For each delta, extract value using variable bit width\n   e. Apply sign extension if needed and add to accumulated value\n   f. Store result to output buffer and advance pointer\n9. Update bit stream reader state with final position and bit counts\n\nParameters:\npDecoderCtx - Pointer to decoder context structure containing:\n  - pCurrentPos/pEndPos: Boundary validation pointers\n  - nCodeWidth: Bit width for value decoding (8-16 bits)\n  - bSignedMode: Flag for signed (1) vs unsigned (0) interpretation  \n  - pOutputBuffer: Destination buffer for decoded short values\npBitReader - Pointer to bit stream reader state containing:\n  - pData: Current position in input data stream\n  - pSaved: Preserved data pointer for restoration\n  - dwBitBuffer: Current 32-bit buffer holding unprocessed bits\n  - dwBitCount: Number of valid bits remaining in buffer\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function updates output buffer and bit reader state in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero initial code triggers fast skip mode for empty data blocks\n- Signed mode uses separate bit for sign rather than two's complement encoding\n- Run-length encoding uses code 0 to repeat previous value N times\n- Bit buffer automatically refills from input stream when exhausted\n- Maximum run length limited to 8 elements per iteration for efficiency\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1F (31) - Bit mask for shift count modulo 32\n0xFFFFFFFF - Full bit mask for 32-bit extraction\n0x20 (32) - Bits per uint for buffer calculations  \n0x21 (33) - Adjusted bit count for signed mode extraction\n0x4 (4) - Bit width for run-length codes\n0x8 (8) - Maximum elements processed per loop iteration\n0xF (15) - Mask for 4-bit length codes\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nDecoderContext (48 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type      Description\n0x00    4     pCurrentPos       void*     Current decode position\n0x04    4     pEndPos          void*     End boundary pointer\n0x08    4     nCodeWidth       uint      Bit width for values (8-16)\n0x0C    4     bSignedMode      uint      Signed interpretation flag\n0x10-0x24 20  reserved         uint[5]   Padding/reserved fields\n0x28    4     nBitOffset       uint      Bit offset configuration\n0x2C    4     pOutputBuffer    short*    Output buffer pointer\n\nBitStreamReader (16 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type      Description\n0x00    4     pData            uint*     Current input data pointer\n0x04    4     pSaved           uint*     Saved data pointer\n0x08    4     dwBitBuffer      uint      32-bit bit accumulator\n0x0C    4     dwBitCount       uint      Valid bits in buffer\n\nError Handling:\n- Returns early if boundary validation fails (pCurrentPos != pEndPos)\n- Bit buffer underflow automatically triggers data refill from input stream\n- No explicit bounds checking on output buffer (caller responsible)\n- Malformed bit stream data may produce undefined behavior",
