      "name": "ConvertYuv422ToRgb",
      "signature": "void ConvertYuv422ToRgb(int nPixelCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts YUV422 planar pixels to RGB format using MMX SIMD instructions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global buffer pointers: chroma U/V pointers, source/destination RGB buffers\n2. Calculate destination address: source buffer base + (pixel count \u00d7 16 bytes per 4 pixels)\n3. Update global source buffer current pointer to new destination\n4. For each pixel group (processes 4 pixels per iteration):\n   a. Load U and V chroma components from planar buffers (16-bit values)\n   b. Extract high and low bytes from chroma values for color channel processing\n   c. Increment chroma buffer pointers by 2 bytes (next U/V pair)\n   d. Load RGB pixel data from destination buffer (32-bit ARGB)\n   e. Extract ARGB color channels using bit shifts (Alpha=bits 24-31, Red=16-23, Green=8-15, Blue=0-7)\n   f. Pack chroma and RGB components using MMX PUNPCKLBW/PUNPCKHBW operations\n   g. Store 8-byte interleaved color data to both source and destination buffers\n   h. Advance buffer pointers by 16 bytes (4 pixels \u00d7 4 bytes each)\n   i. Check if source pointer reached calculated end address\n5. Save updated buffer pointers back to global variables\n6. Return to caller with stack cleanup (__stdcall)\n\nParameters:\nnPixelCount - Number of 4-pixel groups to process (int)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function processes pixels in groups of 4 using MMX 64-bit registers\n- Requires 16-byte alignment for optimal MMX performance\n- Input pixel count is multiplied by 16 (4 pixels \u00d7 4 bytes each)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x4 (4) - Bytes per pixel (32-bit ARGB format)\n0x2 (2) - Bytes per chroma component (16-bit U/V values)\n0x8 (8) - Bytes per MMX register\n0x10 (16) - Bytes per 4-pixel group\n0x18 (24) - Alpha channel bit shift (bits 24-31)\n0x10 (16) - Red channel bit shift (bits 16-23)\n0x8 (8) - Green channel bit shift (bits 8-15)\n\nError Handling:\n- No explicit error checking - assumes valid buffer pointers\n- Relies on caller to ensure sufficient buffer space\n- MMX state not explicitly cleared (caller responsibility)\n\nGlobal Variables Used:\ng_pSrcBufferCurrent (0x100332e0) - Current source RGB buffer pointer\ng_pChromaBufferU (0x100332f0) - U chroma component buffer pointer\ng_pChromaBufferV (0x100332f4) - V chroma component buffer pointer\ng_pSrcBufferEnd (0x100332e8) - End of source buffer pointer\ng_pDstBufferEnd (0x100332ec) - End of destination buffer pointer\ng_pDstBufferCurrent (0x100332e4) - Current destination RGB buffer pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
