      "name": "BinkWait",
      "signature": "uint BinkWait(BinkDecoder * pBinkDecoder)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Implements frame timing and synchronization for Bink video playback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate decoder pointer is not null\n2. Check if decoder is active (flags at offset 0x1fc)\n3. Initialize timing baseline if not set (offset 0x20c)\n4. Process current frame if frame index is valid (offset 0x1e8 != -1)\n5. Get current system time via timeGetTime()\n6. Adjust playback timing and update frame counters\n7. Calculate frame duration based on frame rate and frame count\n8. Compare elapsed time against target frame duration\n9. If timing is ahead, update baseline and frame counter\n10. If callback handler exists and returns non-zero, yield CPU with Sleep(0)\n11. Return 1 to continue playback or 0 if timing requirements met\n\nParameters:\npBinkDecoder - Pointer to BinkDecoder structure containing playback state\n\nReturns:\n0 - Frame timing satisfied, no wait needed\n1 - Continue waiting, frame not ready for display\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1fc (508) - Decoder active flags\n0x20c (524) - Timing baseline timestamp\n0x1e8 (488) - Current frame index (-1 = invalid)\n0x1fc (508) - Frame counter\n0x84 (132) - Previous frame counter\n0x14 (20) - Frame rate denominator\n0x18 (24) - Frame rate numerator\n0x3f (63) - Paused state flag\n0x8b (139) - Skip frame flag\n0x85 (133) - Maximum skip threshold\n0x42 (66) - Callback mode flag\n0x48 (72) - Callback function pointer\n0x44 (68) - Callback context data\n0x20 (32) - Decoder mode flags\n0x8000000 - No sleep flag bit\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x14   | 4    | dwFrameRateDenom | uint | Frame rate denominator\n0x18   | 4    | dwFrameRateNum | uint | Frame rate numerator\n0x20   | 4    | dwModeFlags | uint | Decoder mode and control flags\n0x1e8  | 4    | nCurrentFrame | int | Current frame index (-1 = invalid)\n0x1fc  | 4    | dwFrameCount | uint | Total frames processed\n0x20c  | 4    | dwTimeBaseline | uint | Timing baseline timestamp\n0x210  | 4    | dwPrevFrameCount | uint | Previous frame count for delta\n0x214  | 4    | dwMaxSkipThreshold | uint | Maximum frames to skip when behind",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
