      "name": "ApplyDifferentialEncodingTo8x8Block",
      "signature": "void ApplyDifferentialEncodingTo8x8Block(char * pbDestBuffer, int nDestStride, int * pBitStream, char cMask7Bit, char * pbSourceBlock)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Applies 7-bit differential encoding to an 8x8 pixel block for Bink video compression.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call DecompressBitStreamData to decode 64 differential values from bitstream into local 8x8 array\n2. Extract bit mask from parameter bMask7Bit for 7-bit range limitation (0x7F maximum)\n3. For each pixel in the 8x8 source block (64 total pixels):\n   a. Read source pixel value from pbSourceBlock at offset [0x00-0x3F]\n   b. Read corresponding differential value from decompressed local array\n   c. Add differential to source pixel: dest = source + differential\n   d. Store result in destination buffer at calculated row/column position\n4. Process pixels in specific order: rows 0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7 with stride-based addressing\n5. Use pointer arithmetic to advance through destination buffer by stride increments\n6. Apply row offset calculations: param_2 (stride), param_2*2, param_2*3 for row addressing\n\nParameters:\nlpbDestBuffer - Output buffer for processed 8x8 block (64 bytes)\nnDestStride - Destination buffer stride in bytes per row for 2D addressing\nlpBitStream - Bitstream state structure containing compressed differential data\nbMask7Bit - 7-bit mask value (0x00-0x7F) for differential range limiting\nlpbSourceBlock - Source 8x8 block containing base pixel values (64 bytes)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (modifies destination buffer directly)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nBlock size: Fixed 8x8 pixels (64 bytes total)\nPixel order: Linear addressing [0x00-0x3F] maps to row-column positions\nStride addressing: Uses param_2, param_2*2, param_2*3 for multi-row calculations\n7-bit limitation: bMask7Bit constrains differential range to prevent overflow\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x40 - Total number of pixels in 8x8 block (64 decimal)\n0x3F - Maximum pixel index in 64-byte block\n0x7F - Maximum value for 7-bit mask (127 decimal)\n0x00-0x3F - Linear pixel offsets within source block\n\nError Handling:\nNo bounds checking on buffer access (assumes valid 64-byte blocks)\nNo validation of stride parameter (assumes positive stride values)\nCaller responsible for buffer allocation and size verification\n\nDifferential Encoding:\nSource pixels provide base values, differentials provide signed adjustments\nResult = Source[i] + Differential[i] for each pixel position\nUsed in Bink video codec for block-based compression with motion compensation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
