      "name": "BinkSetSoundSystem",
      "signature": "bool BinkSetSoundSystem(void * pfnSoundCallback, long lSoundParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Set sound system callback function for Bink video playback\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate sound callback function pointer is not NULL\n2. Check if existing sound callback is already registered\n3. If same callback already set, jump directly to invocation\n4. If different callback exists and sound system is busy, return failure\n5. Store new sound callback function pointer in global storage\n6. Invoke sound callback with provided parameter\n7. Store non-zero result as sound system handle\n8. Return true if sound handle is valid, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\npfnSoundCallback (void*): Function pointer to sound system callback that accepts long parameter and returns long handle\nlSoundParam (long): Parameter to pass to sound system callback during initialization\n\nReturns:\nbool: true if sound system was successfully initialized with valid handle, false if NULL callback or initialization failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL callback pointer: Returns false immediately without any sound system changes\n- Existing callback match: Skips re-registration and calls existing callback directly\n- Sound system busy (g_lSoundBusyFlag != 0): Prevents callback changes and returns false\n- Callback returns 0: Sound system handle remains unchanged, function may return false\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1002f670: g_pfnSoundCallback - Global storage for sound callback function pointer\n0x1002f674: g_lSoundHandle - Global storage for sound system handle returned by callback\n0x1002f678: g_lSoundBusyFlag - Global flag indicating if sound system is currently busy\n\nError Handling:\n- NULL parameter validation prevents segmentation faults\n- Busy flag check prevents concurrent sound system modifications\n- Zero return value handling ensures valid sound handle storage",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
