      "name": "ConvertUintToFloat10",
      "signature": "float10 ConvertUintToFloat10(float10 * __return_storage_ptr__, uint dwPackedFloat)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "float10 *",
      "comment": "Converts a packed 32-bit floating-point format to extended precision float10.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract mantissa bits by right-shifting 5 positions and masking with 0x77fffff\n2. Cast mantissa to float10 for extended precision arithmetic\n3. Extract table index from lower 5 bits (dwPackedFloat & 0x1f)\n4. Multiply mantissa by lookup table value at computed index\n5. Check sign bit at position 28 (0x10000000)\n6. If sign bit set, negate the result\n7. Return the computed extended precision value\n\nParameters:\ndwPackedFloat: Packed floating-point value with custom bit layout\n               Bits 0-4:   Table lookup index (0-31)\n               Bits 5-27:  Mantissa value (23 bits)\n               Bit 28:     Sign bit (1=negative, 0=positive)\n               Bits 29-31: Unused/reserved\n\nReturns:\nExtended precision floating-point value (float10) representing the unpacked number\n\nSpecial Cases:\nSign bit (0x10000000) inverts the result sign regardless of mantissa value\nLookup table contains 32 double precision scaling factors for mantissa conversion\nMantissa mask 0x77fffff ensures only valid mantissa bits are processed\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x77fffff - Mantissa extraction mask (bits 5-27, 23 bits total)\n0x1f - Table index mask (bits 0-4, values 0-31)\n0x10000000 - Sign bit mask (bit 28)\n5 - Right shift count to position mantissa after table index bits",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
