      "comment": "Configure absolute screen position and offset parameters for a Bink video buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input buffer pointer - return 0 if NULL\n2. Initialize client point structure with zero coordinates\n3. Convert client coordinates to screen coordinates using window handle at offset 0x60\n4. Calculate absolute screen position by adding offsets to converted coordinates\n5. Store screen X position (converted X + offset X) at buffer offset 0x50\n6. Store original offset X parameter at buffer offset 0x58  \n7. Store screen Y position (converted Y + offset Y) at buffer offset 0x54\n8. Store original offset Y parameter at buffer offset 0x5C\n9. Set high bit flag (0x80000000) in buffer flags field at offset 0x10\n10. Call refresh/update function FUN_10005e00 with zero parameter\n11. Return success code 1\n\nParameters:\n  pBinkBuffer (BinkBuffer *): Pointer to Bink video buffer structure containing window handle and position data\n  nOffsetX (int): X coordinate offset to apply to converted screen position\n  nOffsetY (int): Y coordinate offset to apply to converted screen position\n\nReturns:\n  0: Error - NULL buffer pointer provided\n  1: Success - offset configuration completed successfully\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL buffer validation prevents crash on invalid pointers\n  - Window handle at offset 0x60 must be valid for ClientToScreen conversion\n  - Offset values can be negative for leftward/upward positioning\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name     Type        Description\n0x10    4     dwFlags       uint        Buffer flags (bit 31 set by this function)\n0x50    4     dwScreenX     int         Absolute screen X coordinate\n0x54    4     dwScreenY     int         Absolute screen Y coordinate  \n0x58    4     dwOffsetX     int         Original X offset parameter\n0x5C    4     dwOffsetY     int         Original Y offset parameter\n0x60    4     hWnd          uint        Window handle for coordinate conversion\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x80000000: High bit flag set in buffer flags to indicate offset configuration active\n0x60: Buffer offset containing window handle for ClientToScreen API\n0x50: Buffer offset for absolute screen X coordinate storage\n0x54: Buffer offset for absolute screen Y coordinate storage  \n0x58: Buffer offset for original X offset parameter storage\n0x5C: Buffer offset for original Y offset parameter storage\n0x10: Buffer offset for flags field manipulation",
