      "name": "ConvertChromaToRgbPixels",
      "signature": "void ConvertChromaToRgbPixels(int nPixelPairCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Convert chroma U/V pixel pairs to RGB using lookup table interpolation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store initial chroma buffer pointers for reset operation\n2. Process first loop for current buffer pixel pairs:\n   a. Read U and V chroma values from global buffers, advance pointers\n   b. Use chroma values as indices into conversion lookup tables\n   c. Read Y (luminance) values from destination buffer, advance by 2 bytes\n   d. Combine lookup values using CONCAT operations to form RGB pixels\n   e. Store RGB pixel data to source buffer, advance by 6 bytes\n   f. Decrement pixel pair counter\n3. Reset chroma buffer pointers to saved initial values\n4. Process second loop for end buffer pixel pairs:\n   a. Read U and V chroma values, advance pointers  \n   b. Perform same lookup table conversions as step 2\n   c. Store intermediate pixel pair in global DAT_1002dff0\n   d. Combine with additional RGB data for final pixel output\n   e. Store completed RGB data to end buffer locations\n   f. Decrement remaining pixel counter\n\nParameters:\nnPixelPairCount (int): Number of chroma UV pixel pairs to process\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nLoop processes pixels in pairs for efficient RGB conversion\nUses 5 lookup tables for YUV to RGB color space conversion\nBuffer pointers are global variables maintained between calls\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10033730: Primary U chroma lookup table base address  \n0x10033f30: Secondary U chroma lookup table base address\n0x10033b30: Secondary V chroma lookup table base address\n0x10034330: Primary V chroma lookup table base address\n0x10038b60: Y luminance lookup table base address\n0x1002dff0: Temporary pixel pair storage location",
