      "name": "GenerateTrigLookupTable",
      "signature": "void GenerateTrigLookupTable(int nTableSize, int * pnIndexArray, float * pflLookupTable)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Generates trigonometric lookup tables for FFT (Fast Fourier Transform) operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize index array with table size and set second element to 1\n2. Early exit if table size <= 2 (insufficient for FFT computation)\n3. Calculate half table size for symmetry optimization \n4. Compute pi/2 using arctangent(g_dPiConstant, 1) where g_dPiConstant = 1.0\n5. Initialize first two lookup table entries: [0]=1.0 (cos 0), [1]=0.0 (sin 0)\n6. Calculate base angle step: pi/2 divided by half size\n7. Compute cosine for middle point and store at indices [half] and [half+1]\n8. Forward pass loop: Generate cos/sin pairs for indices 2 through half-2\n   - Calculate angle = step_angle * current_index\n   - Store cos(angle) at forward positions [i] and [i+1] \n   - Store sin(angle) at backward positions using symmetry\n9. Backward copying loop: Mirror values using trigonometric symmetry\n   - Copy from forward half to backward half with index reversal\n   - Exploits cos(\u03c0-x) = -cos(x) and sin(\u03c0-x) = sin(x) identities\n10. Call GenerateBitReversedIndices to create bit-reversed index mapping for FFT\n\nParameters:\nnTableSize - Size of trigonometric lookup table (must be power of 2, minimum 4)\npnIndexArray - Output buffer for bit-reversed indices [size: nTableSize]\npflLookupTable - Output buffer for cos/sin pairs [size: nTableSize] \n\nReturns:\nvoid - Results stored in output buffers pnIndexArray and pflLookupTable\n\nSpecial Cases:\nTable size <= 2: Function exits early, only sets index[0]=size and index[1]=1\nTable size 4: Minimal case with cos/sin for 0\u00b0, 90\u00b0, 180\u00b0, 270\u00b0 \n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1 (1) - Initialization value for second index array element\n0x2 (2) - Minimum threshold for FFT table generation\ng_dPiConstant (1.0) - Mathematical constant for pi/2 calculation via atan(1,1)\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit validation - assumes nTableSize is power of 2 >= 4\nInvalid sizes may cause buffer overruns or incorrect FFT results\nCaller responsible for validating input parameters\n\nStructure Layout:\nIndex Array Layout (pnIndexArray):\nOffset  Size  Field         Type    Description\n0x00    4     tableSize     int     Original table size value  \n0x04    4     stepValue     int     Always set to 1\n0x08    ...   indices       int[]   Bit-reversed indices from GenerateBitReversedIndices\n\nLookup Table Layout (pflLookupTable):\nOffset  Size  Field         Type    Description  \n0x00    4     cos0          float   cos(0) = 1.0\n0x04    4     sin0          float   sin(0) = 0.0\n0x08    4     cos1          float   cos(\u03c0/n)\n0x0C    4     sin1          float   sin(\u03c0/n)\n...     ...   cosPairs      float[] Cosine values for angles 0 to \u03c0/2\n...     ...   sinPairs      float[] Sine values for angles 0 to \u03c0/2",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
