      "name": "FftRadix8DecimationInFrequency",
      "signature": "void FftRadix8DecimationInFrequency(int nLength, int nStride, float * pfData, float * pfTwiddleTable)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Perform 8-point Fast Fourier Transform using radix-8 decimation in frequency butterfly operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract first twiddle factor from twiddle table at offset 8\n2. Perform first radix-8 stage if stride is positive  \n3. Calculate 8 data pointers at stride intervals (0*stride through 7*stride)\n4. Apply radix-8 butterfly operations in groups of 8 complex samples\n5. Combine real/imaginary pairs with twiddle factor multiplication\n6. Store results back to original data array locations\n7. Advance all pointers by 2 floats (1 complex sample)\n8. Repeat until all samples processed in first stage\n9. Process higher radix stages if data length exceeds 8*stride\n10. Extract additional twiddle factors for each higher stage\n11. Apply complex twiddle factor rotations with cos/sin components\n12. Perform nested butterfly operations for each radix stage\n13. Continue until all data processed through complete FFT stages\n\nParameters:\nnLength (int): Total number of complex samples to process\nnStride (int): Stride between data blocks in complex samples  \npfData (float *): Pointer to interleaved real/imaginary data array\npfTwiddleTable (float *): Pointer to precomputed twiddle factor table\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Results stored directly in pfData array",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
