      "name": "CalculateExponentialF2xm1",
      "signature": "undefined5 CalculateExponentialF2xm1(undefined4 flInput, undefined1 byPrecisionFlag)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined5",
      "comment": "Calculate exponential using x86 F2XM1 instruction (2^x-1).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if absolute value of input exceeds maximum threshold constant\n2. If input too large, test if input is negative and return negate if needed\n3. For valid range inputs, extract integer and fractional parts using FRNDINT\n4. Test if rounded value equals zero to determine processing path\n5. Calculate (input - rounded_value) to get fractional component\n6. Apply F2XM1 instruction to absolute value of fractional part\n7. Return 5-byte extended precision floating-point result\n\nParameters:\nflInput (undefined4): Input value passed via ECX register for exponential calculation\nbyPrecisionFlag (undefined1): Precision control flag passed via DL register\n\nReturns:\nundefined5: 5-byte packed floating-point result containing calculated 2^x-1 value\n           High byte contains status flags, low 4 bytes contain calculated result\n\nSpecial Cases:\nInput values exceeding maximum threshold trigger different processing paths\nNegative inputs may trigger sign inversion depending on magnitude\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1002e5ee: g_ldMaxExponentThreshold - Maximum input threshold for F2XM1 range checking\n\nError Handling:\nLarge input values fall back to alternate calculation methods\nFunction maintains FPU state through stack operations and status word checks",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
