      "name": "FormatFloatingPointString",
      "signature": "char * FormatFloatingPointString(uint dwFormatFlags, char * lpszOutputBuffer, uint dwPrecision)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Formats floating-point number into decimal string representation with specified precision and sign handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check global formatting state flag (DAT_1003c8f0) - if false, call FUN_100202f7() to parse float\n2. If in direct mode and precision matches cached value (DAT_1003c8f4), write simple \"0\" with null terminator\n3. Extract sign flag from parsed data - if negative (0x2d), prepend '-' to output buffer\n4. Handle integral part - if exponent < 1, write single '0', otherwise advance write position by exponent value\n5. If precision > 0, append decimal point character from DAT_1002e918\n6. Handle fractional part - if exponent negative, pad with leading zeros using _memset with '0' (0x30)\n7. Return pointer to completed string buffer\n\nParameters:\ndwFormatFlags (uint): Formatting control flags (currently unused parameter)\nlpszOutputBuffer (char*): Output buffer to receive formatted decimal string\ndwPrecision (uint): Number of decimal places to include in output\n\nReturns:\nlpszOutputBuffer - Pointer to the formatted string buffer (same as input parameter)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
