      "name": "ProcessChromaPixelLines",
      "signature": "int ProcessChromaPixelLines(int nWidth, int nHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Processes chroma pixel lines for color conversion by interleaving U/V components with destination pixels.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter from input width parameter (nWidth)\n2. Loop until all pixels processed (width decremented by 2 each iteration):\n   a. Extract chroma U byte from g_pChromaBufferU pointer\n   b. Extract chroma V byte from g_pChromaBufferV pointer  \n   c. Extract destination pixel byte from g_pDstBufferCurrent pointer\n   d. Concatenate chroma components into 3-byte value using CONCAT operations\n   e. Create 32-bit pixel value by combining chroma and destination data\n   f. Apply chroma mask (0xff00ff) and shift operations for pixel alignment\n   g. Store processed pixels to both source buffers (current and end)\n   h. Store duplicate pixels with stride offset using g_dwPixelStride\n   i. Advance all buffer pointers (chroma +1, destination +2, source +2)\n3. Return sum of original width and height parameters\n\nParameters:\nnWidth - Number of pixel pairs to process (width/2)\nnHeight - Secondary dimension parameter for return calculation\n\nReturns:\nSum of nWidth + nHeight (appears to be total pixel count calculation)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nLoop processes 2 pixels per iteration, so width should be even\nFunction assumes all global buffer pointers are valid and properly initialized\nChroma buffers advance by single bytes while pixel buffers advance by pairs\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xff00ff - Chroma component mask for U/V extraction\n0x10 - 16-bit left shift for pixel component alignment \n0x8 - 8-bit left shift for byte positioning\n0x2 - Pixel pair increment (2 pixels processed per loop)\n0x4 - Secondary pixel offset in destination buffer\n\nError Handling:\nNo bounds checking on buffer access\nNo validation of input parameters\nAssumes proper buffer alignment and sufficient memory",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
