      "name": "BinkBufferUpdateDisplayRegion",
      "signature": "void BinkBufferUpdateDisplayRegion(BinkBuffer * pBuffer, int nUpdateMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Updates Bink video buffer display region with window visibility check and screen clipping.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if buffer display flag (offset 0x64) is enabled, exit if disabled\n2. Validate window visibility using IsWindowVisible on buffer's window handle (offset 0x60)\n3. Load source coordinates from buffer (offsets 0x0, 0x4)\n4. Load positioning offsets from buffer (offsets 0x50, 0x54) for clipping calculations\n5. Handle negative positioning offsets by converting to positive clipping values\n6. Calculate destination rectangle by adding buffer dimensions (offsets 0x3c, 0x40) to positioning\n7. Perform screen boundary clipping against g_nScreenWidth and g_nScreenHeight\n8. Validate final clipping bounds ensure visible region exists\n9. Set buffer display mode flag (offset 0x6c) based on nUpdateMode parameter\n10. Call D3D interface blit method (vtable offset 0x84) with calculated parameters\n11. If window invisible or clipping invalid, call D3D clear method instead\n\nParameters:\npBuffer    - Pointer to BinkBuffer structure containing video data and display settings\nnUpdateMode - Display update mode (1 = normal/paused, 2 = active/playing, others = unchanged)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If buffer display flag disabled (pBuffer[0x19] == 0): exits immediately\n- If window not visible: calls D3D clear method with null parameters  \n- If final clipping bounds invalid: calls D3D clear method\n- nUpdateMode == 1: sets buffer mode to paused (0x6c = 0)\n- nUpdateMode == 2: sets buffer mode to playing (0x6c = 1)\n- Other nUpdateMode values: leaves mode unchanged\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x38   - D3D parameter structure size indicator\n0x200  - Base D3D rendering flags  \n0x800  - Additional D3D rendering option\n0x3e00 - Conditional flag mask applied when buffer mode active\n0x84   - D3D interface vtable offset for blit/clear method\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type  | Description\n0x00   | 4    | nSourceX      | int   | Source X coordinate  \n0x04   | 4    | nSourceY      | int   | Source Y coordinate\n0x3c   | 4    | nBufferWidth  | int   | Buffer width dimension\n0x40   | 4    | nBufferHeight | int   | Buffer height dimension  \n0x48   | 4    | pD3DInterface | void* | Direct3D interface pointer\n0x50   | 4    | nOffsetX      | int   | X positioning offset (can be negative)\n0x54   | 4    | nOffsetY      | int   | Y positioning offset (can be negative)\n0x60   | 4    | hWindow       | HWND  | Window handle for visibility check\n0x64   | 4    | fDisplayFlag  | int   | Display enabled flag\n0x6c   | 4    | nDisplayMode  | int   | Display mode (0=paused, 1=active)",
