      "name": "ExpandPixelDataWithAlpha",
      "signature": "int ExpandPixelDataWithAlpha(int nPixelCount, int nAdditionalValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Expands pixel data by duplicating bytes from destination buffers to source buffers with alpha channel values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter from pixel count parameter\n2. For each iteration, decrement counter by 2 (processes 2 pixels per iteration)\n3. Read byte from destination buffer current position\n4. Create 32-bit value by duplicating byte to high/low 16-bits and OR with 0x80008000 alpha mask\n5. Write expanded value to source buffer current position\n6. Advance destination buffer pointer by 2 bytes, read next byte\n7. Create second 32-bit expanded value and write to source buffer current+4\n8. Repeat process for destination buffer end and source buffer end pointers\n9. Advance all buffer pointers by 8 bytes (2 uint32 values)\n10. Continue loop while remaining pixel count > 0\n11. Return sum of original parameters\n\nParameters:\nnPixelCount (int): Number of pixels to process (decremented by 2 each iteration)\nnAdditionalValue (int): Additional value added to return result\n\nReturns:\nint: Sum of nPixelCount + nAdditionalValue\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x80008000 - Alpha channel mask applied to both high/low 16-bit portions\n0x10 - Left shift amount to move byte to high 16 bits\n2 - Pixels processed per iteration\n8 - Total bytes advanced per iteration (4 bytes * 2 buffers)\n\nGlobal Buffer Usage:\ng_pDstBufferCurrent - Source of pixel data being read and expanded\ng_pDstBufferEnd - Secondary source buffer for pixel data\ng_pSrcBufferCurrent - Destination for expanded pixel data\ng_pSrcBufferEnd - Secondary destination for expanded pixel data",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:e8938b232dc428549f2aa90498091d98",
