      "name": "BinkBufferUnlock",
      "signature": "int BinkBufferUnlock(BinkBuffer * pBinkBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Unlocks a Bink video buffer and updates display regions after video operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pBinkBuffer parameter is not NULL, return 0 if invalid\n2. Retrieve interface pointer from buffer offset 0x48 \n3. If interface exists:\n   - Call interface method at offset 0x80 with buffer parameter at 0x78\n   - If cursor restore needed (flag at 0x70), call BinkRestoreCursor with handle at 0x74\n   - Clear position fields at offsets 0x14 and 0x18\n   - Update display region with mode 2\n4. If no interface but special flag set at 0x8c:\n   - Clear position fields at offsets 0x14 and 0x18\n5. Clear lock bit (0x80000000) from flags at offset 0x10\n6. Return success status 1\n\nParameters:\npBinkBuffer (BinkBuffer *): Pointer to Bink buffer structure to unlock\n\nReturns:\nint: 1 for success, 0 if buffer parameter is NULL\n\nSpecial Cases:\nBuffer validation prevents crashes from NULL pointers\nInterface method call uses virtual function table dispatch\nCursor restoration only occurs when flag 0x70 is non-zero\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x48 (72): Offset to interface pointer in BinkBuffer\n0x78 (120): Offset to parameter for interface method call\n0x70 (112): Offset to cursor restore flag\n0x74 (116): Offset to cursor handle\n0x14 (20): Offset to X position field  \n0x18 (24): Offset to Y position field\n0x8c (140): Offset to special processing flag\n0x10 (16): Offset to lock/status flags\n0x80: Offset to virtual method in interface vtable\n0x80000000: Lock bit mask in status flags\n2: Display update mode parameter\n\nError Handling:\nNULL buffer parameter returns 0 immediately\nNo error checking on interface method calls or BinkRestoreCursor\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type    | Description\n-------|------|---------------|---------|----------------------------------\n0x10   | 4    | dwStatusFlags | uint    | Lock status and control flags\n0x14   | 4    | nXPosition    | int     | Horizontal position coordinate\n0x18   | 4    | nYPosition    | int     | Vertical position coordinate  \n0x48   | 4    | pInterface    | void*   | Pointer to unlock interface\n0x70   | 4    | dwCursorFlag  | uint    | Cursor restoration needed flag\n0x74   | 4    | hCursor       | void*   | Handle for cursor restoration\n0x78   | 4    | pMethodParam  | void*   | Parameter for interface method\n0x8c   | 4    | dwSpecialFlag | uint    | Special processing mode flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ecef6e0b279551dbbcf95cc18e5c85a1",
