      "name": "CaptureExceptionHandlerState",
      "signature": "void CaptureExceptionHandlerState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Captures processor state during exception handling for unwinding and debugging\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Preserve general-purpose registers (EBX, ECX) on stack\n2. Load base address of global exception handler state structure (0x1002e450)\n3. Store first stack parameter (return address) into dwStackParameter field (+8)\n4. Store EAX register value into dwEaxRegister field (+4)\n5. Store EBP frame pointer into dwEbpRegister field (+12)\n6. Restore general-purpose registers from stack\n7. Return to caller with 4-byte stack cleanup\n\nParameters:\n\nIMPLICIT nEaxRegister (int): EAX register value at function entry\nIMPLICIT nEbpRegister (int): EBP frame pointer value at function entry\nIMPLICIT [EBP + 8] (int): Stack parameter containing return address or exception info\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No explicit return value, modifies global exception handler state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nFunction uses __stdcall calling convention with 4-byte stack cleanup (RET 0x4)\nDirect register access without formal parameters in function signature\nGlobal state structure must be pre-allocated at 0x1002e450\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nOffset | Size | Field Name         | Type | Description\n-------|------|-------------------|------|----------------------------------\n+0     | 4    | dwFlags           | uint | Status flags (not accessed here)\n+4     | 4    | dwEaxRegister     | uint | Saved EAX register value\n+8     | 4    | dwStackParameter  | uint | Stack parameter/return address  \n+12    | 4    | dwEbpRegister     | uint | Saved EBP frame pointer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x1002e450 - Base address of global ExceptionHandlerState structure\n0x4 - Offset to dwEaxRegister field in exception state\n0x8 - Offset to dwStackParameter field in exception state  \n0xc - Offset to dwEbpRegister field in exception state\n0x4 - Stack cleanup bytes for __stdcall convention",
