      "name": "SetConfigurationMode",
      "signature": "void SetConfigurationMode(int nModeValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets global configuration mode based on input parameter value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if mode value equals 1 (single player/campaign mode)\n2. If true, set global configuration to 0x21 (33) and return\n3. Check if mode value is 2 or 3 (multiplayer variants)  \n4. If true, set global configuration to 0x22 (34) and return\n5. For all other values, leave global configuration unchanged\n\nParameters:\n  nModeValue (int): Configuration mode selector\n                   1 = Campaign/single player mode (sets to 0x21)\n                   2-3 = Multiplayer mode variants (sets to 0x22)\n                   Other = No configuration change\n\nReturns:\n  void: Function has no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Invalid mode values (0, negative, >3) result in no configuration change\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x21 (33): Campaign/single player configuration mode\n  0x22 (34): Multiplayer configuration mode",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ed5d8332b54d28b982dbc31e264d087d",
