      "name": "UpdateProcessingCounterWithTiming",
      "signature": "void UpdateProcessingCounterWithTiming(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Updates processing counter using high-resolution timing measurements and bit field operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read current processing counter flags from global variable\n2. Check if timing mode enabled (bit 2, value 0x04)\n3. Read high-resolution timestamp using RDTSC instruction\n4. Calculate elapsed time since last measurement\n5. Check if precision timing mode enabled (bit 1, value 0x02)\n6. Extract 5-bit step index from bits 3-7 of counter\n7. Compare elapsed time with threshold from bits 8+ of counter\n8. Based on timing and step index, update counter with new value:\n   - If time exceeded: increment step index (max 0x1F)\n   - If time not exceeded: decrement step index (min 0)\n   - Apply bit masking to maintain 8-byte alignment (& 0xF8)\n9. If precision mode disabled: encode timing into upper 8 bits with flags\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, modifies global processing counter directly\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x04 - Timing mode enable flag (bit 2)\n0x02 - Precision timing mode flag (bit 1)  \n0x1F - Maximum step index (5-bit field: 31 decimal)\n0xF8 - Step alignment mask (maintains 8-byte boundaries)\n0xFD - Flag preservation mask (clears bit 1)\n0x100 - Shift factor for encoding timing in upper 8 bits\n0x03 - Reset value for step index when at minimum\n0x01 - Reset value for counter when at maximum step\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If timing mode disabled: function returns immediately\n- Step index 0x1F (maximum): resets counter to 0x01\n- Step index 0 (minimum): sets counter to 0x03\n- Time threshold exceeded: increments step with alignment\n- Time threshold not met: decrements step with alignment\n\nError Handling:\nFunction operates on global state with no validation or error reporting",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f1b0856acf5d358573d7e9dbd470c8df",
