      "name": "GetFpuStatusWord",
      "signature": "int GetFpuStatusWord(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Retrieves the current FPU (Floating Point Unit) status word as an integer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store current FPU status word to local stack location using FSTSW instruction\n2. Sign-extend 16-bit status word to 32-bit integer\n3. Return the status word value in EAX register\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nint - Current FPU status word containing condition codes, exception flags, \n      and control information. Bit layout follows x87 FPU specification:\n      - Bits 0-5: Exception flags (IE, DE, ZE, OE, UE, PE)\n      - Bits 6-7: Stack fault (SF) and Error summary status (ES)  \n      - Bits 8-10: Condition codes C0, C1, C2\n      - Bits 11-13: Top of stack pointer (TOP)\n      - Bit 14: Condition code C3\n      - Bit 15: FPU busy flag (B)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function operates directly on FPU hardware state\n- No error conditions possible - always returns current status\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x2 (stack offset): Local storage location for 16-bit status word",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f75de985f89ec0796fb5e3ad0eeb7130",
