      "name": "ProcessFpuExceptionHandler",
      "signature": "void ProcessFpuExceptionHandler(uint dwExceptionCode, int * pExceptionParams, ushort * pwFpuControlWord)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Process FPU exception handling based on exception type and control parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract FPU control word value from pointer parameter\n2. Decode exception type from pExceptionParams[0] using switch-case logic\n3. Map exception types to FPU flag values:\n   - Type 1,5: Flag 0x08 (Invalid Operation)\n   - Type 2: Flag 0x04 (Denormal Operand)\n   - Type 3: Flag 0x11 (Overflow + Invalid Operation)\n   - Type 4: Flag 0x12 (Overflow + Denormal)\n   - Type 8: Flag 0x10 (Overflow)\n   - Type 7: Reset exception type to 1 and skip processing\n4. Call ProcessFloatControlFlags to validate FPU state\n5. If validation successful, prepare exception context:\n   - For special codes (0x10, 0x16, 0x1d): Set operand flags and enable precision mode\n   - For other codes: Clear precision bit\n6. Invoke RaiseFpuException with complete context\n7. Update FPU control word with SetFpuControlWordBits\n8. Perform validation and configuration finalization\n\nParameters:\n  dwExceptionCode - Exception code identifying type of FPU error\n  pExceptionParams - Pointer to exception parameter array containing:\n    [0] Exception type (1-8)\n    [2-3] First operand (double)\n    [4] Second operand flags  \n    [5] Reserved field\n    [6-7] Second operand (double)\n  pwFpuControlWord - Pointer to FPU control word for updates\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, updates FPU state through parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Exception type 7: Resets to type 1 and bypasses flag processing\n  Invalid types: Skip to control word finalization\n  Validation failure: Skip exception raising, proceed to finalization\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x04 - Denormal operand flag\n  0x08 - Invalid operation flag  \n  0x10 - Overflow flag\n  0x11 - Overflow + Invalid operation\n  0x12 - Overflow + Denormal\n  0x16 - Underflow exception code\n  0x1d - Precision loss exception code\n  0xffffffe3 - Control flags mask (clear bits 2-4)\n  0x03 - Precision control bits (extended precision)\n  0xfffffffe - Clear precision enable bit",
