      "name": "FormatFloatAsExponential",
      "signature": "char * FormatFloatAsExponential(double * pValue, char * lpszOutput, int nPrecision, bool fUpperCase)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Converts floating-point value to exponential notation string (e.g., \"1.234e+02\").\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Parse floating-point value using FUN_100202f7() or use cached result\n2. Initialize output formatting with FUN_10020280() or FUN_1001e274()\n3. Handle negative sign: if result indicates negative, prepend '-' character\n4. Format mantissa: insert decimal point and precision digits if nPrecision > 0\n5. Append exponent template \"e+000\" using FUN_10020190()\n6. Convert to uppercase 'E' if fUpperCase flag is set\n7. Format exponent value: extract exponent from parsing result, adjust by -1\n8. Handle negative exponent: negate value and set '-' sign\n9. Format exponent digits: convert hundreds, tens, and units digits to ASCII\n10. Return pointer to formatted output string\n\nParameters:\n  pValue - Pointer to double-precision floating-point value to convert\n  lpszOutput - Output buffer to receive formatted exponential string\n  nPrecision - Number of decimal places to display after decimal point\n  fUpperCase - Boolean flag: true for 'E', false for 'e' in exponent\n\nReturns:\n  Pointer to formatted output string (same as lpszOutput parameter)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero precision: omits decimal point and fractional digits\n  - Negative values: prepends minus sign to mantissa\n  - Large exponents: handles values requiring 3-digit exponent formatting\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x2d (45) - ASCII minus sign character\n  0x45 (69) - ASCII uppercase 'E' for exponent\n  0x30 (48) - ASCII '0' character for zero comparison\n  100 (0x64) - Threshold for 3-digit exponent formatting\n  10 (0x0A) - Threshold for 2-digit exponent formatting\n\nError Handling:\n  - Assumes valid input parameters and sufficient output buffer space\n  - Relies on helper functions for floating-point parsing and formatting\n  - No explicit error checking or validation performed\n\nStructure Layout:\nFloatParseResult (16 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name       Type     Description\n  +0x00   4     dwSignFlag       uint     Sign indicator (0x2d for negative)\n  +0x04   4     nExponent        int      Exponent value from parsing\n  +0x08   4     reserved1        uint     Reserved field\n  +0x0C   4     szExponentString char *   Pointer to exponent string",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
