      "name": "BinkOpenMiles",
      "signature": "void * BinkOpenMiles(void * pBink)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Initializes Bink video decoder with Miles Audio Interface Library support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pBink handle parameter (return null if null)\n2. Check if instance is already cached in global table at offset 0x18\n3. If cached instance matches parameter, proceed to step 7\n4. If cached instance exists but different, check error flag and return null if set\n5. Cache the new instance handle in global table\n6. Check if Miles Audio function pointers are already loaded\n7. If not loaded, dynamically load MSS32.DLL library with error mode suppression\n8. Validate library handle (must be > 0x20 for valid HMODULE)\n9. Load all required AIL (Audio Interface Library) function pointers via GetProcAddress\n10. Set fallback function pointer for _AIL_digital_latency@4 if not found (0x1001abb0)\n11. Validate at least one critical function loaded (_AIL_minimum_sample_buffer_size@12)\n12. Return interface function table pointer (0x1001a780) on success, null on failure\n\nParameters:\npBink - Handle to Bink video decoder instance (void *)\n\nReturns:\nvoid * - Pointer to Bink-Miles interface function table on success\nnull - If initialization failed or invalid parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\nInstance caching prevents multiple initialization attempts for same Bink handle\nError flag DAT_1003c87c prevents re-initialization after failure\nLibrary loading uses SEM_FAILCRITICALERRORS (0x8000) to suppress error dialogs\nFallback function provided for optional _AIL_digital_latency@4 API\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8000 - SEM_FAILCRITICALERRORS flag for SetErrorMode\n0x20 - Minimum valid HMODULE value (system DLL range check)\n0x18 - Instance cache offset in g_adFloatConversionTable global array\n0x1001a780 - Address of Bink-Miles interface function table\n0x1001abb0 - Fallback function for digital latency calculation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
