      "comment": "Tests if a cursor appears in software-rendered mode versus hardware cursor.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if software cursor detection is enabled via GetSystemMetrics(SM_SWAPBUTTON)\n2. Initialize local buffer arrays and call Bink video interface to get frame data\n3. Cache previous cursor detection results in global variables for performance\n4. If cached results match current cursor and dimensions, return cached value\n5. Create temporary invisible window \"MouseTypeWind\" for cursor testing\n6. Get current cursor position and convert to window client coordinates\n7. Hide cursor completely by calling ShowCursor(0) repeatedly until hidden\n8. Sample pixel color at cursor position using GetPixel() with cursor hidden\n9. Restore cursor and show it by calling ShowCursor(1) repeatedly\n10. Lock Bink buffer and write test pattern to frame buffer at cursor location\n11. Hide cursor again and sample same pixel position for color comparison\n12. Compare hidden pixel color vs visible pixel color to detect software cursor\n13. Clean up temporary window, restore cursor, and cache detection results\n14. Return 1 if cursor affects pixel rendering (software), 0 if not (hardware)\n\nParameters:\nparam_1 (HCURSOR): Handle to cursor being tested for software rendering detection\n\nReturns:\nReturns uint: 1 if cursor renders in software mode affecting pixel buffer\n             0 if cursor renders in hardware mode without affecting pixels\n             0 if detection is disabled or fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic Number 0x887601c2: Bink video error code indicating buffer unavailable\n- Magic Number 0x13: GetSystemMetrics parameter SM_SWAPBUTTON for detection toggle  \n- Magic Number 0x200: Window class style CS_OWNDC for device context ownership\n- Magic Number 0x90000000: Window style WS_POPUP | WS_DISABLED for invisible window\n\nStructure Layout:\nWNDCLASSA structure (offset 0x2c):\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type        Description\n0x00    4     style               UINT        Window class style (0x200 = CS_OWNDC)\n0x04    4     lpfnWndProc         WNDPROC     Window procedure (LAB_10005820)\n0x08    4     cbClsExtra          int         Extra class bytes (0)\n0x0c    4     cbWndExtra          int         Extra window bytes (0)\n0x10    4     hInstance           HINSTANCE   Module handle\n0x14    4     hIcon               HICON       Class icon (NULL)\n0x18    4     hCursor             HCURSOR     Class cursor (test cursor)\n0x1c    4     hbrBackground       HBRUSH      Background brush (NULL)\n0x20    4     lpszMenuName        LPCSTR      Menu name (NULL)\n0x24    4     lpszClassName       LPCSTR      Class name (\"MouseTypeWind\")\n\nGlobal Cache Variables:\nDAT_1002f154: Previous cursor handle for result caching\nDAT_1002f158: Previous width value for cache validation\nDAT_1002f15c: Previous height value for cache validation  \nDAT_1002ef08: Cached detection result (1=software, 0=hardware)\n\nError Handling:\n- Returns 0 if GetSystemMetrics indicates detection disabled\n- Returns 0 if Bink buffer operations fail with error codes\n- Handles ShowCursor() return values to ensure proper cursor state restoration\n- Cleans up window resources even if pixel sampling fails",
