      "name": "BinkBufferOpen",
      "signature": "uint * BinkBufferOpen(HWND hWnd, uint dwWidth, uint dwHeight, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint *",
      "comment": "Creates and initializes a Bink video buffer for hardware-accelerated video playback\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters (width and height must be non-zero)\n2. Extract surface type (bits 0-4) and alpha flags (bits 24-31) from dwFlags\n3. If surface type is 2 (YUV overlay), attempt YUV overlay initialization\n4. Otherwise, initialize DirectDraw subsystem and iterate through surface types\n5. For each surface type, attempt to create appropriate DirectDraw/Direct3D surface\n6. Test surface compatibility and set surface flags based on capabilities\n7. If hardware acceleration fails, fall back to software DIB section rendering\n8. Allocate and zero-initialize BinkBuffer structure (164 bytes)\n9. Set buffer dimensions, window handle, and surface properties\n10. Calculate window coordinates relative to desktop and client area\n11. Initialize offset and scaling parameters\n12. Attach DirectDraw surface if available\n\nParameters:\nhWnd - Window handle for video output (HWND)\ndwWidth - Video buffer width in pixels (uint)\ndwHeight - Video buffer height in pixels (uint)\ndwFlags - Buffer creation flags with embedded surface type and options (uint)\n\nReturns:\nPointer to initialized BinkBuffer structure on success\nNULL on failure (invalid parameters, insufficient resources, or unsupported configuration)\n\nSurface Types (bits 0-4 of dwFlags):\n0x00 - Default surface type (tries multiple formats)\n0x01 - RGB surface (software fallback)\n0x02 - YUV overlay surface (hardware YUV)\n0x03 - YUY2 surface format\n0x04 - UYVY surface format\n0x05 - YV12 surface format\n\nAlpha Channel Flags (bits 24-31 of dwFlags):\n0xFF000000 - Full alpha channel support\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x32315659 - FOURCC code for 'YV12' planar YUV format\n0x32595559 - FOURCC code for 'YUY2' packed YUV format\n0x59565955 - FOURCC code for 'UYVY' packed YUV format\n0x4000000 - DirectDraw surface flag\n0x8000000 - Direct3D texture surface flag\n0xFF000000 - Alpha channel capability mask\n\nError Handling:\nReturns NULL for zero width or height\nReturns NULL if DirectDraw initialization fails\nReturns NULL if no compatible surface format found\nCleans up allocated resources on failure\nSets global error message in DAT_1002f01c buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\nUses software DIB section if video memory depth > 1 and hardware fails\nHandles both windowed and fullscreen rendering modes\nSupports cursor visibility detection for overlay modes\nCalculates 32-byte aligned stride for optimal memory access",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
