      "name": "ValidateBinkInstallLocation",
      "signature": "int ValidateBinkInstallLocation(HMODULE hModule, int nReason)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Validates BinkW32.DLL installation location during DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if reason is DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH (1), return 1 if not\n2. Store module handle in global g_hBinkModule for later use\n3. Get full module path using GetModuleFileNameA with 127 char buffer\n4. Find last path separator (backslash or colon) by scanning backwards\n5. Null-terminate path to extract directory portion only\n6. Get Windows directory path using GetWindowsDirectoryA\n7. Compare module directory with Windows directory using case-insensitive comparison\n8. If not in Windows directory, check System directory using GetSystemDirectoryA\n9. If not in System directory either, return 1 (success - proper location)\n10. If found in Windows or System directory, show error message and return 0\n\nParameters:\nhModule - Handle to BinkW32.DLL module being loaded\nnReason - DLL load reason code (DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH = 1, DLL_PROCESS_DETACH = 0)\n\nReturns:\n1 - Success, DLL can be loaded (not in Windows/System directories or other reason codes)\n0 - Failure, DLL incorrectly installed in Windows or System directory\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Only validates on DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH, ignores other reason codes\n- Uses case-insensitive path comparison via __strcmpi\n- Scans backwards from end to find last path separator (handles both \\\\ and : characters)\n- Shows user-friendly error dialog when incorrect installation detected\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1 (1 decimal) - DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH constant\n0x7f (127 decimal) - Maximum path buffer length minus null terminator\n0x5c (92 decimal) - ASCII backslash character '\\'\n0x3a (58 decimal) - ASCII colon character ':'\n0x10 (16 decimal) - MB_ICONERROR flag for MessageBoxA",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:c0ad15467707cfe32300724cf778aa20",
