      "name": "BinkOpenDirectSound",
      "signature": "pointer BinkOpenDirectSound(int nMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "pointer",
      "comment": "Initialize DirectSound subsystem for Bink video playback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if DirectSound mode already set and matches requested mode\n2. If different mode requested and system is busy, return failure\n3. Store new DirectSound mode in global state variable\n4. If mode is 0 (hardware DirectSound), initialize DirectSound library:\n   a. Set DirectSound initialized flag to 1\n   b. Load DSOUND.DLL if not already loaded (with error suppression)\n   c. Get DirectSoundCreate function pointer from loaded DLL\n   d. Return NULL if DirectSoundCreate unavailable\n5. If mode is non-zero (software mode), reset DirectSound state\n6. Call internal Bink DirectSound initialization function\n7. Call cleanup/setup function and return success callback pointer\n\nParameters:\n  nMode (int): DirectSound mode selector\n    - 0 = Hardware DirectSound mode (loads DSOUND.DLL)\n    - Non-zero = Software audio mode (no DirectSound)\n\nReturns:\n  pointer: Function pointer to Bink DirectSound callback or NULL\n    - Success: Returns address of BinkDirectSoundHandler (0x1001c080)\n    - Failure: Returns NULL if DirectSound unavailable or initialization failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Mode change while system busy (g_fDirectSoundBusy != 0) returns NULL\n- DSOUND.DLL load failure returns NULL\n- DirectSoundCreate API unavailable returns NULL\n- Magic number 0x8000: SEM_NOOPENFILEERRORBOX flag for SetErrorMode\n- Magic number 0x1f: Minimum valid HMODULE value check\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x8000: SEM_NOOPENFILEERRORBOX - Suppress file error dialogs during DLL load\n- 0x1f: HMODULE threshold - Values below 32 indicate DLL load failure\n\nError Handling:\n- Uses SetErrorMode to suppress error dialogs during DSOUND.DLL loading\n- Validates HMODULE return value to detect LoadLibraryA failures  \n- Returns NULL for any initialization failure to indicate error to caller\n\nGlobal State Variables:\n- g_nDirectSoundMode: Current DirectSound mode (-1 = uninitialized)\n- g_fDirectSoundBusy: System busy/lock flag (prevents mode changes)\n- g_fDirectSoundInit: DirectSound initialized flag (1 = hardware, 0 = software)\n- g_hDSoundModule: DSOUND.DLL module handle (HMODULE)\n- g_pfnDirectSoundCreate: DirectSoundCreate function pointer (FARPROC)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:fabd94e72423594605c6945b67ac4454",
